reignObject></g><g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fg-color:#4D4D4D;" color="#4D4D4D" fill="#4D4D4D" stroke="#4D4D4D" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 205.66 151.12)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-fo-width:3.65em;--ltx-fo-height:0.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.17em;font-size:8.19pt;" color="#000000" height="8.72" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.78)" width="41.43"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.F2.pic1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\subsetneq\ \cdots\ \nearrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#4D4D4D;" mathcolor="#4D4D4D" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.410em">⊊</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#4D4D4D;" mathcolor="#4D4D4D" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.410em">⋯</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#4D4D4D;" mathcolor="#4D4D4D" mathsize="0.700em">↗</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\subsetneq\ \cdots\ \nearrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#262626;--ltx-fill-color:#262626;--ltx-fg-color:#262626;" color="#262626" fill="#262626" stroke="#262626" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 24.57 -29.33)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:58.55em;--ltx-fo-height:0.61em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.17em;font-size:7.97pt;" height="8.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="645.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><a href="#A4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma D.3 (Fresh-index availability). ‣ The exhaustive generator and the separation () ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a><span id="S3.F2.pic1.17" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">: every finite </span><math id="S3.F2.pic1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.F2.pic1.18" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;"> sits inside some chain element, so the
adversary can pose the dilemma at ever-larger </span><math id="S3.F2.pic1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.F2.pic1.19" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">, forever.</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g></g></symbol></pattern></defs></g></svg></span>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 2</span>: </span><span id="S3.F2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The engine of the separation. The targets form a Gold chain
<math id="S3.F2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}\subsetneq H_{2}\subsetneq\cdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⊊</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">⊊</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}\subsetneq H_{2}\subsetneq\cdots</annotation></semantics></math> (bars) with union <math id="S3.F2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> (top); each
chain element misses an infinite tail <math id="S3.F2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\geq j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\geq j}</annotation></semantics></math> (hatched). Sound coverage of
the union forces the output set <math id="S3.F2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> (dashed band) to cover all of <math id="S3.F2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> but the
finite seen-set; sound coverage of a chain element forces the same <math id="S3.F2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> inside
<math id="S3.F2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. off its tail. The band over the hatched region (outlined) is
the contradiction (<a href="#A4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma D.2 (Sandwich-exclusion). ‣ The exhaustive generator and the separation () ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>), and non-identifiability
(<a href="#A4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma D.3 (Fresh-index availability). ‣ The exhaustive generator and the separation () ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a>) lets the adversary pose the dilemma infinitely often.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3.2</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(The exhaustive generator and the separation)<span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In the pair model with the protocol of <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem3" title="Definition 2.3 (Pair model). ‣ The nested model: validity versus value ‣ The Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>:</span></p>
<ol id="S3.I2" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:2.2em;">
<li id="S3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">(Exhaustive generator)</span><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> With the verifier </span><math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}_{F}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the generator
</span><math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{n}=F\setminus S_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{n}=F\setminus S_{n}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> achieves sound coverage in the limit on every countable
pair model: at every round, it has zero hallucination, and (when </span><math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\setminus H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\setminus H</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is
infinite) infinitely many trivia.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">(Separation)</span><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> There is a countable pair model </span><math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (all
languages infinite, every </span><math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}\setminus H_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}\setminus H_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> infinite) on which no oracle-free
set-valued generator (an arbitrary function of the prefix) achieves sound coverage in the
limit.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The verifier strictly enlarges the class of pair models admitting sound coverage, from
a proper subclass to all of them; this is in contrast to breadth, where within a fiber it
adds nothing </span><span id="S3.I2.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text">(<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1 (Verification is not taste). ‣ Verification is not taste ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>(c))</span><span id="S3.I2.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof sketch.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Part (a) is immediate from <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\subseteq F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\subseteq F</annotation></semantics></math>. For (b), the model <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math> is
built on a Gold-style chain <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}\subsetneq H_{2}\subsetneq\cdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⊊</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">⊊</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}\subsetneq H_{2}\subsetneq\cdots</annotation></semantics></math> with union <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> in
the collection. A sandwich-exclusion lemma (<a href="#A4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma D.2 (Sandwich-exclusion). ‣ The exhaustive generator and the separation () ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>; <a href="#S3.F2" title="In Sound coverage: what the verifier does buy ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) shows no
output set can sound-cover both the union <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(F_{\infty},L^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(F_{\infty},L^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> and a chain element <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(F_{j},H_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(F_{j},H_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> against the same finite seen-set; a fresh-index lemma (<a href="#A4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma D.3 (Fresh-index availability). ‣ The exhaustive generator and the separation () ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a>) keeps the
chain non-identifiable. An adaptive phase construction then forces any oracle-free generator
to fail on one of the realized instances; the construction is a <em id="S3.SS2.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">non-effective</em>
adversary, the standard convention for impossibility results in this line
(<a href="#S2.Thmtheorem4" title="Definition 2.4 (Verifier oracle). ‣ The nested model: validity versus value ‣ The Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a>). Part (c) combines (a) and (b). Full proof in <a href="#A4.SS2" title="The exhaustive generator and the separation () ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 3.3</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(Two regimes in part (c))<span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Where the oracle identifies the ambient (and hence the target), as on <math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math>,
whose fibers are singletons, it suffices for sound coverage, and its absence makes sound
coverage impossible. Within a non-singleton fiber, by contrast, the oracle adds nothing about
which target is valuable (<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1 (Verification is not taste). ‣ Verification is not taste ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>(d)), so there its power is exactly to keep the
unavoidable overshoot inside <math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>: relocating errors from false to trivial, reducing neither
their number nor locating value.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#1F4FA8;">The trivia phase transition</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Throughout this subsection the ambient is <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and the verifier is the constant
function: the dichotomy is a verifier-free theorem about nested targets. The verifier’s role
in the paper is settled by <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1 (Verification is not taste). ‣ Verification is not taste ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorems</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 3.2 (The exhaustive generator and the separation). ‣ Sound coverage: what the verifier does buy ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, and what follows quantifies the
value/trivia tradeoff that remains after verification is granted.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F3" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S3.F3.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="209.76" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 417.29 209.76" width="417.29"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,209.76) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(54.62,0) translate(0,47.9)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 294.83 0"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 292.57 0)"><path d="M 5.9 0 L 0.89 1.87 L 2.4 0 L 0.89 -1.87 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 218.87 -43.28)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6.92em;--ltx-fo-height:0.65em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="7.69" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="81.36"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S3.F3.pic1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">trivia allowance</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 137.35"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.0 1.0 -1.0 0.0 0 135.09)"><path d="M 5.9 0 L 0.89 1.87 L 2.4 0 L 0.89 -1.87 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -4.95 149.56)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.75em;--ltx-fo-height:0.65em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="91.16"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S3.F3.pic1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">optimal coverage <math id="S3.F3.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.76 39.37 L 2.76 39.37"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -34.98 36.6)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.09em;--ltx-fo-height:0.71em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.24em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.3)" width="24.54"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.F3.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">α</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha/2</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.76 110.24 L 2.76 110.24"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -50.01 107.47)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.36em;--ltx-fo-height:0.71em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.24em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.3)" width="39.57"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.F3.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\alpha/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.800em">−</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">α</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\alpha/2</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 41.3 -15.34)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.03em;--ltx-fo-height:0.65em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="7.69" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="59.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S3.F3.pic1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">finite count</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 165.89 -23.65)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 18.76)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 7.69)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 16.18 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.86em;--ltx-fo-height:0.65em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="7.69" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="68.94"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S3.F3.pic1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">infinite count</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 15.99)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.33em;--ltx-fo-height:0.71em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.24em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.3)" width="86.26"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S3.F3.pic1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(any rate, even </span><math id="S3.F3.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.800em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.F3.pic1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000099;--ltx-fill-color:#000099;--ltx-fg-color:#000099;" color="#000099" fill="#000099" stroke="#000099" stroke-width="1.2pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 5.91 39.37 L 141.73 39.37"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#4D4D1F;--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D1F;--ltx-fg-color:#4D4D00;" color="#4D4D00" fill="#4D4D1F" stroke="#4D4D1F" stroke-width="1.2pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 145.67 110.24 L 287.4 110.24"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000099;--ltx-fill-color:#000099;--ltx-fg-color:#000099;" color="#000099" fill="#000099" stroke="#000099"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 141.73 39.37 M 143.95 39.37 C 143.95 40.59 142.96 41.58 141.73 41.58 C 140.51 41.58 139.52 40.59 139.52 39.37 C 139.52 38.15 140.51 37.16 141.73 37.16 C 142.96 37.16 143.95 38.15 143.95 39.37 Z M 141.73 39.37"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#4D4D1F;--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;--ltx-fg-color:#4D4D00;" color="#4D4D00" fill="#FFFFFF" stroke="#4D4D1F"><path d="M 145.67 110.24 M 147.88 110.24 C 147.88 111.46 146.89 112.45 145.67 112.45 C 144.45 112.45 143.46 111.46 143.46 110.24 C 143.46 109.01 144.45 108.02 145.67 108.02 C 146.89 108.02 147.88 109.01 147.88 110.24 Z M 145.67 110.24"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#808080;--ltx-fill-color:#808080;--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" color="#808080" fill="#808080" stroke="#808080" stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,2.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 143.7 39.37 L 143.7 110.24"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;--ltx-fg-color:#4D4D4D;" color="#4D4D4D" fill="#4D4D4D" stroke="#4D4D4D"><path style="fill:none" d="M 175.2 110.24 M 175.2 110.24 C 177.27 109.2 178.66 106.78 178.66 103.32 L 178.66 81.72 C 178.66 78.26 180.04 75.84 182.12 74.8 C 180.04 73.77 178.66 71.34 178.66 67.88 L 178.66 46.29 C 178.66 42.83 177.27 40.41 175.2 39.37"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#202020;--ltx-fill-color:#202020;--ltx-fg-color:#202020;" color="#202020" fill="#202020" stroke="#202020" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 193.12 68.18)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 18.08)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 6.52)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.58em;--ltx-fo-height:0.59em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.17em;font-size:7.97pt;" height="8.4" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.52)" width="28.47"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S3.F3.pic1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">jump </span><math id="S3.F3.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=1-\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.700em">=</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.700em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=1-\alpha</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 15.66)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.07em;--ltx-fo-height:0.61em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:7.97pt;" height="6.73" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="22.81"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S3.F3.pic1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">the </span><em id="S3.F3.pic1.9" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;">unrecorded mass</em><span id="S3.F3.pic1.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;"> </span><math id="S3.F3.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(H\setminus C,H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">H</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∖</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">C</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">H</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(H\setminus C,H)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000080;--ltx-fill-color:#000080;--ltx-fg-color:#000080;" color="#000080" fill="#000080" stroke="#000080" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 4.86 50.12)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 16.41)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 6.73)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 36.44 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.39em;--ltx-fo-height:0.61em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:7.97pt;" height="6.73" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="59.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S3.F3.pic1.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">KW frontier</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 13.99)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.78em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.22em;font-size:7.97pt;" height="9.69" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.26)" width="8.65"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S3.F3.pic1.12" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">(</span><a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Fact 2.1 (Partial-enumeration generation; ( , , Theorem 1.6 in arXiv version)). ‣ Partial enumeration and the revealed core ‣ The Model" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fact</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a><span id="S3.F3.pic1.13" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#404020;--ltx-fill-color:#404020;--ltx-fg-color:#404000;" color="#404000" fill="#404020" stroke="#404020" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 139.64 125.5)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.22em;font-size:7.97pt;" height="9.75" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.33)" width="26.91"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.F3.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">G</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{*}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.F3.pic1.14" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">  (</span><a href="#S3.Thmtheorem7" title="Theorem 3.7 (Achievability side: sweep and the tight generator). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.7</span></a><span id="S3.F3.pic1.15" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 3</span>: </span><span id="S3.F3.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The trivia phase transition (<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem10" title="Corollary 3.10 (The trivia dichotomy). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Corollary</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.10</span></a>). The optimum
jumps by exactly the unrecorded mass <math id="S3.F3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> as the trivia allowance
crosses from finite to infinite <em id="S3.F3.5.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">count</em>; the rate at which trivia are
emitted is irrelevant, and the right endpoint is attained by the single
generator <math id="S3.F3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> at vanishing rate. The colors are the title’s: blue for the
raced core, gold for the harvested surplus.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We now price the relocation exactly, in the partial (density) model. The setting is a single
family on which the optimal guaranteed coverage is determined — and on which a sharp
dichotomy appears: with only finitely many trivia the optimum is <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha/2</annotation></semantics></math>, and allowing
infinitely many trivia (even at rate tending to <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>) jumps it to <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\alpha/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\alpha/2</annotation></semantics></math>. The
transition is in trivia <em id="S3.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">count</em>, not rate.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">The tight family.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We work over <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> in numeric order. Let <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}\coloneqq\{\text{evens}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext>evens</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}\coloneqq\{\text{evens}\}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}[j]=2(j-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}[j]=2(j-1)</annotation></semantics></math> be the formal world’s coverable part, and for a target density <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>
define</p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\coloneqq\{\,K^{\prime}[\lceil k/\alpha\rceil]:k\geq 1\,\}\subsetneq K^{\prime},\qquad D\coloneqq K^{\prime}\setminus K,\qquad F=\mathbb{N}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊊</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∖</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\coloneqq\{\,K^{\prime}[\lceil k/\alpha\rceil]:k\geq 1\,\}\subsetneq K^{\prime},\qquad D\coloneqq K^{\prime}\setminus K,\qquad F=\mathbb{N}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The family is <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{\alpha}\coloneqq\{K,K^{\prime}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{\alpha}\coloneqq\{K,K^{\prime}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> the sparse <em id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">revealed</em> target and <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>
the full coverable world. The point of (<a href="#S3.E1" title="Equation 3.1 ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>) is that it realizes <em id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">exact</em>
density for <em id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">every</em> real <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, not merely rational <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert K\cap K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N]\rvert=\lfloor\alpha N\rfloor\quad\text{for all }N,\qquad\text{hence}\qquad d(K,K^{\prime})=\alpha\text{ exactly}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mtext>hence</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> exactly</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert K\cap K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N]\rvert=\lfloor\alpha N\rfloor\quad\text{for all }N,\qquad\text{hence}\qquad d(K,K^{\prime})=\alpha\text{ exactly},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and moreover <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\cap K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N]=K[1\!\dots\!m_{N}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\cap K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N]=K[1\!\dots\!m_{N}]</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{N}=\lfloor\alpha N\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{N}=\lfloor\alpha N\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>,
while <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\setminus K^{\prime}=\{\text{odds}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∖</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext>odds</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\setminus K^{\prime}=\{\text{odds}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is infinite. The two readings <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> share a
single transcript when the adversary enumerates <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, which is what makes the caps bind for
every generator. Here <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> plays the role of the valuable target <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> that of the
coverable part of <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\setminus K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∖</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\setminus K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> (the odd column) is the inexhaustible trivia
reservoir; the verifier is inert since <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> is known.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The lower bounds rest on a self-contained race lemma (<a href="#S3.F4" title="In The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>). It says two things at
once: a generator following a greedy “race” rule covers at least half of a target, and an
adversary running a “racing” enumeration caps <em id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">every</em> generator at half.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.4</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(The racing adversary)<span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For infinite <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\subseteq U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\subseteq U</annotation></semantics></math>, the <em id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">racing adversary</em> <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> enumerates, at every round
<math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\neq 2^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\neq 2^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prec" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≺</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prec</annotation></semantics></math>-least element of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\setminus(S_{t-1}\cup O_{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\setminus(S_{t-1}\cup O_{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math> (the
least string unused by either side), and at every round <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=2^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=2^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> the <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prec" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≺</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prec</annotation></semantics></math>-least element of
<math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(O_{t-1}\cap K)\setminus S_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∩</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(O_{t-1}\cap K)\setminus S_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, recycling a generator-claimed element so that the
enumeration stays complete (falling back to the fresh rule if no such element exists).</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.5</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Race lemma)<span id="S3.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\subseteq U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\subseteq U</annotation></semantics></math> be infinite and let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mathrm{race}}\subseteq\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>race</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mathrm{race}}\subseteq\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> have density
<math id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, with</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(t)\coloneqq t-\lvert T_{\mathrm{race}}\cap[1\dots t]\rvert=o(t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>race</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(t)\coloneqq t-\lvert T_{\mathrm{race}}\cap[1\dots t]\rvert=o(t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<ol id="S3.I3" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:2.2em;">
<li id="S3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(R1)</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">(Greedy cover)</span><span id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> If at every </span><math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in T_{\mathrm{race}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>race</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in T_{\mathrm{race}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> the generator outputs
the </span><math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prec" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≺</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prec</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-least element of </span><math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\setminus(S_{t}\cup O_{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\setminus(S_{t}\cup O_{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then against every
adversary enumeration, </span><math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert O\cap K[1\!\dots\!M]\rvert\geq\tfrac{1}{2}\,(M-w(\tau_{M})-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert O\cap K[1\!\dots\!M]\rvert\geq\tfrac{1}{2}\,(M-w(\tau_{M})-1)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for
all </span><math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, where </span><math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{M}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is the index of the </span><math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-th race round; hence </span><math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{d}(O\cap K,K)\geq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{d}(O\cap K,K)\geq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(R2)</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">(Racing cap)</span><span id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> The racing adversary </span><math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{K}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> of </span><a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Definition 3.4 (The racing adversary). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a><span id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a legal
repetition-free enumeration of </span><math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Against it, every generator satisfies </span><math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert O\cap K[1\!\dots\!M]\rvert\leq M/2+\log_{2}M+3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert O\cap K[1\!\dots\!M]\rvert\leq M/2+\log_{2}M+3</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for </span><math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">; hence </span><math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{d}(O\cap K,K)\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{d}(O\cap K,K)\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof sketch.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">For (R1), at any race round with <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K[1\!\dots\!M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K[1\!\dots\!M]</annotation></semantics></math> not yet resolved the greedy output is a new
element of <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\cap K[1\!\dots\!M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\cap K[1\!\dots\!M]</annotation></semantics></math> (the <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prec" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≺</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prec</annotation></semantics></math>-least unresolved element of <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> lies in the
downward-closed <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K[1\!\dots\!M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K[1\!\dots\!M]</annotation></semantics></math>); counting contributions against “steals” into the seen-set
gives the bound. For (R2), the racing adversary alternates fresh enumeration with recycling
the generator’s hoarded elements; an injection from output-elements to fresh-enumerated
elements, with <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\log M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\log M)</annotation></semantics></math> exceptions at powers of two, gives the cap. Full proof in
<a href="#A4.SS3" title="The race lemma () ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
