C 300.62 21.5 302.08 22.33 304.15 22.33 L 313.96 22.33 C 316.03 22.33 317.49 23.16 318.11 24.41"></path><path style="fill:none" d="M 321.26 24.41 M 321.26 24.41 C 321.67 23.16 322.64 22.33 324.02 22.33 L 324.02 22.33 C 325.39 22.33 326.36 21.5 326.77 20.26 C 327.19 21.5 328.15 22.33 329.53 22.33 L 329.53 22.33 C 330.91 22.33 331.87 23.16 332.28 24.41"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 64.27 8.35)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.83em;--ltx-fo-height:0.55em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:7.36pt;" height="5.63" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.63)" width="8.47"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A3.F9.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{9}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathsize="0.500em">a</mi><mn mathsize="0.500em">9</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{9}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 179.23 8.35)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.83em;--ltx-fo-height:0.55em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:7.36pt;" height="5.63" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.63)" width="8.47"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A3.F9.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{9}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathsize="0.500em">a</mi><mn mathsize="0.500em">9</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{9}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 256.39 8.35)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.83em;--ltx-fo-height:0.55em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:7.36pt;" height="5.63" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.63)" width="8.47"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A3.F9.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathsize="0.500em">a</mi><mn mathsize="0.500em">3</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{3}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 295.76 8.35)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.83em;--ltx-fo-height:0.55em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:7.36pt;" height="5.63" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.63)" width="8.47"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A3.F9.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathsize="0.500em">a</mi><mn mathsize="0.500em">3</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{3}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 324.09 11.01)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.53em;--ltx-fo-height:0.29em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:7.36pt;" height="2.98" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 2.98)" width="5.36"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A3.F9.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.500em">a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 374.97 23.73)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 23.52)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 10.38)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:13.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.94em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.31em;font-size:7.97pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="148.91"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A3.F9.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert a^{25}\rvert_{G\cup D_{3}}=s_{3}(25)=5&gt;\log_{2}26" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi><mn mathsize="0.700em">25</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">G</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∪</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">D</mi><mn mathsize="0.700em">3</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">s</mi><mn mathsize="0.700em">3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">25</mn><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">5</mn><mo mathsize="0.700em">&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">log</mi><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">26</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert a^{25}\rvert_{G\cup D_{3}}=s_{3}(25)=5&gt;\log_{2}26</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.F9.pic1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">:</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 21.1)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:16.63em;--ltx-fo-height:0.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.22em;font-size:7.97pt;" height="9.69" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.26)" width="183.44"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A3.F9.pic1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#666666;">not compressible (just misses the cut)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g></g></svg></span>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 9</span>: </span><span id="A3.F9.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Wrapped length and the compressibility cut, by example
(<a href="#A3.SS2" title="The macro framework ‣ Appendix C Mathematical Background" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>; <math id="A3.F9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, geometric dictionary <math id="A3.F9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{3}=\{a^{3},a^{9},a^{27},\dots\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>9</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>27</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{3}=\{a^{3},a^{9},a^{27},\dots\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.F9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=1</annotation></semantics></math>). The wrapped length is the base-<math id="A3.F9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> digit sum
(<a href="#A3.E2" title="Equation C.2 ‣ The macro framework ‣ Appendix C Mathematical Background" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>): <math id="A3.F9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{27}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>27</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{27}</annotation></semantics></math> compresses to a single macro and passes the cut,
while <math id="A3.F9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{25}=a^{9}a^{9}a^{3}a^{3}a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>25</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>9</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>9</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{25}=a^{9}a^{9}a^{3}a^{3}a</annotation></semantics></math> needs five symbols and just misses it.
Compressibility is thin, which is the precision phenomenon
<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 4.3 (Imprecision of exhaustive generation). ‣ Case Study: Instantiation in a Compression Model of Mathematics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a> quantifies.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The <em id="A3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">compressibility cut</em> is the threshold</p>
<table id="A3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\kappa}(L)\coloneqq\kappa\log_{2}(1+L)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\kappa}(L)\coloneqq\kappa\log_{2}(1+L),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">and the <em id="A3.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">compressible sublanguage</em> is</p>
<table id="A3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{D}\coloneqq\left\{\,w:\lvert w\rvert_{G\cup D}\leq\theta_{\kappa}(\lvert w\rvert_{G})\,\right\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">{</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{D}\coloneqq\left\{\,w:\lvert w\rvert_{G\cup D}\leq\theta_{\kappa}(\lvert w\rvert_{G})\,\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">the elements whose wrapped length is logarithmic in their raw length. A <em id="A3.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">bounded cut</em>
<math id="A3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\equiv 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\equiv 1</annotation></semantics></math> (used in <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 4.2 (Free-monoid pairs realize the dichotomy). ‣ Case Study: Instantiation in a Compression Model of Mathematics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>(i)) collapses <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{D,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{D,1}</annotation></semantics></math> to the nameable corpus
<math id="A3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\cup D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\cup D</annotation></semantics></math> itself.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We are explicit about the ledger: the framework supplies definitions (macros, wrapped length,
geometric dictionaries) and the motivating asymmetry between <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, and nothing
more. The proofs in <a href="#A4.SS6" title="The instantiation (, and ) ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.6</span></a> are self-contained; no ABFM theorem is invoked.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#1F4FA8;">The usage of ABFM models in the case study</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S4" title="Case Study: Instantiation in a Compression Model of Mathematics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> uses these objects in two shapes. In <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> it builds
<em id="A3.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">refinement chains</em>: nesting the geometric dictionaries by <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{t+1}\subseteq D_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{t+1}\subseteq D_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> gives
a descending chain of compressible languages <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{D_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{D_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> separated by digit-sum witnesses
(<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1 (Abelian refinement chains are identifiable). ‣ Case Study: Instantiation in a Compression Model of Mathematics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>). In <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> it builds <em id="A3.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">name-cut pairs</em>: words <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{i}a\,x^{q+1-i}a\,x^{2^{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></msup></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{i}a\,x^{q+1-i}a\,x^{2^{m}}</annotation></semantics></math> whose unique parsing lets an <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>-position cut the corpus into a sparse target <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and
a full world <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> at any rational density (<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 4.2 (Free-monoid pairs realize the dichotomy). ‣ Case Study: Instantiation in a Compression Model of Mathematics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Deferred Proofs</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix restates each result with its original number and gives the full proof.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#1F4FA8;">Verification is not taste (<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1 (Verification is not taste). ‣ Verification is not taste ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>)</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A4.SS1.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="32.78" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 670 32.78" width="670"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,32.78) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><clipPath id="pgfcp24"><path d="M -22670.54 -22670.54 L 22670.54 -22670.54 L 22670.54 22670.54 L -22670.54 22670.54 Z M 0 4.72 L 0 28.06 C 0 30.67 2.12 32.78 4.72 32.78 L 665.28 32.78 C 667.89 32.78 670 30.67 670 28.06 L 670 4.72 C 670 2.12 667.89 0 665.28 0 L 4.72 0 C 2.12 0 0 2.12 0 4.72 Z"></path></clipPath><g fill-rule="evenodd"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F3F7FC;" fill="#F3F7FC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.72 L 0 28.06 C 0 30.67 2.12 32.78 4.72 32.78 L 665.28 32.78 C 667.89 32.78 670 30.67 670 28.06 L 670 4.72 C 670 2.12 667.89 0 665.28 0 L 4.72 0 C 2.12 0 0 2.12 0 4.72 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#6284C2;--ltx-fill-color:#6284C2;--ltx-fg-color:#6284C2;" color="#6284C2" fill="#6284C2" stroke="#6284C2" stroke-width="1.5pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 1.04 32.78 L 1.04 0"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.62 12.93)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:46.45em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="642.74"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A4.SS1.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:46.45em;">
<span id="A4.SS1.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">See <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1 (Verification is not taste). ‣ Verification is not taste ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove (a) and (b) together (necessity, then sufficiency), then (c) and (d) and the edge
cases.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Necessity.</span> Suppose some fiber <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{F^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{F^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math> violates the relevant condition. Write <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}\coloneqq\mathcal{P}_{F^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>≔</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}\coloneqq\mathcal{P}_{F^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math>; it is countable, nonempty, and all its members are infinite. Restrict the
adversary to instances <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(F^{*},H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(F^{*},H)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>. On every such instance the
verifier handed to a relativized generator <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is always the single fixed function <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}_{F^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}_{F^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the oracle-stripped ordinary generator</p>
<table id="A4.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}_{n}(S_{n})\coloneqq G_{n}^{\,\mathbf{1}_{F^{*}}}(S_{n})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}_{n}(S_{n})\coloneqq G_{n}^{\,\mathbf{1}_{F^{*}}}(S_{n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">This is well defined: in round <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> the generator’s adaptive query tree has finite depth, and
the fixed function <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}_{F^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}_{F^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math> resolves every query, selecting one leaf and one
output. Thus <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is an arbitrary set-valued function of the prefix, exactly the object KMV
quantify over (<a href="#S2.Thmtheorem7" title="Fact 2.7 (Breadth characterizations; ( , , Theorems 3.3 and 3.8)). ‣ Restated characterizations (cited facts). ‣ The nested model: validity versus value ‣ The Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fact</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.7</span></a>; their Remark 2.3 imposes no computability). Extensional
agreement holds across all of <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>: for every fiber instance and every enumeration,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{n}^{\,\mathbf{1}_{F_{z}}}(S_{n})=G^{\prime}_{n}(S_{n})\quad\text{for all }n" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{n}^{\,\mathbf{1}_{F_{z}}}(S_{n})=G^{\prime}_{n}(S_{n})\quad\text{for all }n</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(<math id="A4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="*" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">*</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">because <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{z}=F^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{z}=F^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> indexing a member of the fiber, so the oracle is the
identical function. Now if <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> achieved exact (resp. approximate) breadth in the limit on all
of <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>, then by (<a href="#A4.Ex1" title="Equation 
                  
                    ∗ ‣ Proof. ‣ Verification is not taste () ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                  
                    ∗
                  
                </span> ‣ <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>) the ordinary generator <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> would achieve it on every
target in <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, contradicting <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem7" title="Fact 2.7 (Breadth characterizations; ( , , Theorems 3.3 and 3.8)). ‣ Restated characterizations (cited facts). ‣ The nested model: validity versus value ‣ The Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fact</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.7</span></a>, since <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> violates Angluin’s (resp. the
weak Angluin) condition. Hence the condition is necessary in each part.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sufficiency.</span> Assume every fiber satisfies the relevant condition.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Stage 1 (ambient identification; sample-independent).</em><span id="A4.SS1.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text"> In round <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> the generator
queries the canonical point <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> to the verifier. Call index <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> <em id="A4.SS1.p5.1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">ambient-consistent at
<math id="A4.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math></em> if <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}\cap\{x_{1},\dots,x_{n}\}=F\cap\{x_{1},\dots,x_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}\cap\{x_{1},\dots,x_{n}\}=F\cap\{x_{1},\dots,x_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{z}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{z}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>
be the least ambient-consistent index (the set is nonempty since the true index <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>
qualifies).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Stage-1 stabilization)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{z}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{z}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> stabilizes in finite time to <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{0}\coloneqq\min\{i:F_{i}=F\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{0}\coloneqq\min\{i:F_{i}=F\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text"> is ambient-consistent at every <math id="A4.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A4.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{z}_{n}\leq z_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{z}_{n}\leq z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> always. Each <math id="A4.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&lt;z_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&lt;z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> has
<math id="A4.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}\neq F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}\neq F</annotation></semantics></math> (by minimality of <math id="A4.SS1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>), hence there is a least canonical point <math id="A4.SS1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{m(i)}\in F_{i}\mathbin{\triangle}F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">△</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{m(i)}\in F_{i}\mathbin{\triangle}F</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.SS1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is permanently inconsistent from round <math id="A4.SS1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(i)</annotation></semantics></math> on.
Taking <math id="A4.SS1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{1}\coloneqq\max_{i&lt;z_{0}}m(i)&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{1}\coloneqq\max_{i&lt;z_{0}}m(i)&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, every <math id="A4.SS1.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&lt;z_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&lt;z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is eliminated by round
<math id="A4.SS1.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A4.SS1.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{z}_{n}=z_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{z}_{n}=z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.SS1.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq N_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq N_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. (No distinctness of the <math id="A4.SS1.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is needed;
duplicates share the fiber.)
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Stage 2 (fiber generation).</em><span id="A4.SS1.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text"> For each ambient set <math id="A4.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> that occurs, fix, by the
achievability half of <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem7" title="Fact 2.7 (Breadth characterizations; ( , , Theorems 3.3 and 3.8)). ‣ Restated characterizations (cited facts). ‣ The nested model: validity versus value ‣ The Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fact</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.7</span></a> applied to the fiber <math id="A4.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, an ordinary
generator <math id="A4.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma^{(F)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma^{(F)}</annotation></semantics></math> achieving exact (resp. approximate) breadth in the limit on
<math id="A4.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>. (The choice ranges over the countably many occurring ambient sets; we use the
axiom of choice over this countable index, removable by taking the <math id="A4.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prec" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≺</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prec</annotation></semantics></math>-lexicographically
least generator in a fixed enumeration; see the closing remark.) The constructions’ internal
mechanics are absorbed into the fixed function level; no computability is claimed.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define the composite relativized generator</span></p>
<table id="A4.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{n}^{\,\mathbf{1}_{F}}(S_{n})\coloneqq\Gamma^{(F_{\hat{z}_{n}})}_{n}(S_{n})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mi>F</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{n}^{\,\mathbf{1}_{F}}(S_{n})\coloneqq\Gamma^{(F_{\hat{z}_{n}})}_{n}(S_{n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A4.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq N_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq N_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma D.1 (Stage-1 stabilization). ‣ Proof. ‣ Verification is not taste () ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a> gives <math id="A4.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\hat{z}_{n}}=F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\hat{z}_{n}}=F</annotation></semantics></math>, so</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{n}^{\,\mathbf{1}_{F}}(S_{n})=\Gamma^{(F)}_{n}(S_{n})\quad\text{for }n\geq N_{1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mi>F</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{n}^{\,\mathbf{1}_{F}}(S_{n})=\Gamma^{(F)}_{n}(S_{n})\quad\text{for }n\geq N_{1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(<math id="A4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dagger" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>†</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dagger</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">The true target <math id="A4.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=H_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=H_{z}</annotation></semantics></math> lies in the true fiber <math id="A4.SS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> (witnessed by <math id="A4.SS1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>), and
<math id="A4.SS1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the genuine prefix of a genuine KM enumeration of <math id="A4.SS1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>: the generator never
restarts the enumeration at <math id="A4.SS1.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the guarantee of <math id="A4.SS1.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma^{(F)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma^{(F)}</annotation></semantics></math> there is a finite
round <math id="A4.SS1.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{*}_{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{*}_{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> from which the breadth property holds; for <math id="A4.SS1.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq\max(N_{1},n^{*}_{\Gamma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq\max(N_{1},n^{*}_{\Gamma})</annotation></semantics></math>,
(<a href="#A4.Ex2" title="Equation 
                  
                    † ‣ Proof. ‣ Verification is not taste () ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                  
                    †
                  
                </span> ‣ <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>) transfers it to <math id="A4.SS1.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>. The pre-stabilization rounds form a finite prefix,
absorbed by “in the limit”. This proves (a) and (b).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(c).</span> In the single-ambient case the verifier is the fixed function <math id="A4.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> from
round <math id="A4.SS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, so (<a href="#A4.Ex1" title="Equation 
                  
                    ∗ ‣ Proof. ‣ Verification is not taste () ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                  
                    ∗
                  
                </span> ‣ <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>) gives relativized <math id="A4.SS1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iff" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iff</annotation></semantics></math> oracle-free, and both <math id="A4.SS1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iff" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iff</annotation></semantics></math> (weak)
Angluin by <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem7" title="Fact 2.7 (Breadth characterizations; ( , , Theorems 3.3 and 3.8)). ‣ Restated characterizations (cited facts). ‣ The nested model: validity versus value ‣ The Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fact</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.7</span></a>. Thus, for the breadth goal, the verifier’s only information
content in the pair model is the identification of <math id="A4.SS1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> performed in Stage 1; within a fiber
it changes nothing. (The scope is essential: <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 3.2 (The exhaustive generator and the separation). ‣ Sound coverage: what the verifier does buy ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> shows that for the
sound-coverage goal the verifier does strictly more.)</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(d).</span> For <math id="A4.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{i},H_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{i},H_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> in the same fiber, <math id="A4.SS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}_{F_{i}}=\mathbf{1}_{F_{j}}=\mathbf{1}_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}_{F_{i}}=\mathbf{1}_{F_{j}}=\mathbf{1}_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> literally. The adaptive query tree, resolved by <math id="A4.SS1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> on a fixed prefix
<math id="A4.SS1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, yields the identical path and identical output regardless of which of <math id="A4.SS1.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{i},H_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{i},H_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is the true target. Hence any behavioral distinction within a fiber is driven by the
enumeration alone.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Edge cases.</span> <span id="A4.SS1.p11.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">(E1) Duplicates.</span> Angluin’s conditions are properties of the underlying set system and
are invariant under repetition of languages in the collection. <span id="A4.SS1.p11.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">(E2) Finite fibers.</span> A
finite fiber satisfies Angluin’s condition: for each ordered pair <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{i}\setminus H_{j}\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{i}\setminus H_{j}\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>, place a witness <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{ij}\in H_{i}\setminus H_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{ij}\in H_{i}\setminus H_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> into the
tell-tale <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (at most <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m-1</annotation></semantics></math> elements for a fiber of size <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>); then any <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{j}\supseteq T_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⊇</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{j}\supseteq T_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> forces <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{i}\subseteq H_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{i}\subseteq H_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is not a proper subset of <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<span id="A4.SS1.p11.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">(E3)</span> Only occurring ambients are ever guessed, and occurring fibers are nonempty
(they contain the realized target). <span id="A4.SS1.p11.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">(E4)</span> The same valuable language appearing under
two different ambients constitutes two different instances in two different fibers; Stage 1
separates them by the ambient query.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Choice avoidance.</span> The use of the axiom of choice in Stage 2 is cosmetic. Fix once and for all a canonical
enumeration of all ordinary generators (e.g. a <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prec" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≺</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prec</annotation></semantics></math>-lexicographic order on finite
descriptions); for each occurring ambient <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma^{(F)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma^{(F)}</annotation></semantics></math> be the
lexicographically least generator achieving the required breadth on <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>. This is a
definable choice, so no appeal to the axiom of choice is needed.
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#1F4FA8;">The exhaustive generator and the separation (<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 3.2 (The exhaustive generator and the separation). ‣ Sound coverage: what the verifier does buy ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>)</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first record the two structural lemmas underlying the separation, then give the phase
construction.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.2</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Sandwich-exclusion)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Work over <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=\mathbb{N}\times\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=\mathbb{N}\times\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}=U_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}=U_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (column <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>), let the spine be the
even column-<math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> indices <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=\{(2m,0):m\geq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=\{(2m,0):m\geq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and set <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{j}=L^{*}\setminus R_{\geq j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{j}=L^{*}\setminus R_{\geq j}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\geq j}=\{(2m,0):m\geq j\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\geq j}=\{(2m,0):m\geq j\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{j}=H_{j}\cup A_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{j}=H_{j}\cup A_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\infty}=L^{*}\cup A_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\infty}=L^{*}\cup A_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{j},A_{\infty}\subseteq U_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{j},A_{\infty}\subseteq U_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> (column <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>) infinite. Then for
every <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, every finite <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subseteq U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subseteq U</annotation></semantics></math>, and every <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\subseteq U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\subseteq U</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> cannot
satisfy both</span></p>
<ol id="A4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:2.2em;">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}\setminus S\subseteq G\subseteq F_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∖</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}\setminus S\subseteq G\subseteq F_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{j}\setminus S\subseteq G\subseteq F_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{j}\setminus S\subseteq G\subseteq F_{j}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose both hold. From the lower side of (i) and the upper side of (ii), <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}\setminus S\subseteq G\subseteq F_{j}=H_{j}\cup A_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∖</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}\setminus S\subseteq G\subseteq F_{j}=H_{j}\cup A_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Intersect with <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (column <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>): since
<math id="A4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}\subseteq U_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}\subseteq U_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{j}\subseteq U_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{j}\subseteq U_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> are disjoint columns,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}\setminus S=(L^{*}\setminus S)\cap U_{0}\subseteq(H_{j}\cup A_{j})\cap U_{0}=H_{j}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∖</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∖</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}\setminus S=(L^{*}\setminus S)\cap U_{0}\subseteq(H_{j}\cup A_{j})\cap U_{0}=H_{j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}\setminus H_{j}\subseteq S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}\setminus H_{j}\subseteq S</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\geq j}\subseteq S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\geq j}\subseteq S</annotation></semantics></math>. But <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\geq j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\geq j}</annotation></semantics></math> is infinite and <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is finite, a contradiction. (The set <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> is never used; the
contradiction lives entirely in column <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>.)
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.3</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Fresh-index availability)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">With the parameters of <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma D.2 (Sandwich-exclusion). ‣ The exhaustive generator and the separation () ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>: for every finite <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\subseteq L^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\subseteq L^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and every <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> there is <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq N</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\subseteq H_{j}\subsetneq L^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⊊</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\subseteq H_{j}\subsetneq L^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}\setminus H_{j}=R_{\geq j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}\setminus H_{j}=R_{\geq j}</annotation></semantics></math> infinite. Consequently <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{H_{j}\}_{j}\cup\{L^{*}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{H_{j}\}_{j}\cup\{L^{*}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is a Gold-style ascending
chain with union <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, non-identifiable from positive data, and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> violates Angluin’s
condition in this collection.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is finite, <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\cap R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\cap R</annotation></semantics></math> is finite, so for all sufficiently large <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\cap R_{\geq j}=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\cap R_{\geq j}=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\subseteq L^{*}\setminus R_{\geq j}=H_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\subseteq L^{*}\setminus R_{\geq j}=H_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>; any such <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq N</annotation></semantics></math> works. For every <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\geq j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\geq j}</annotation></semantics></math> is infinite, so <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{j}\subsetneq L^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⊊</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{j}\subsetneq L^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> with infinite
difference; and <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> contains all the odd column-<math id="A4.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> indices, so it is infinite. The chain
is ascending, <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}\subseteq H_{2}\subseteq\cdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">⊆</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}\subseteq H_{2}\subseteq\cdots</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigcup_{j}H_{j}=L^{*}\setminus\bigcap_{j}R_{\geq j}=L^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">∖</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋂</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigcup_{j}H_{j}=L^{*}\setminus\bigcap_{j}R_{\geq j}=L^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. This is the textbook non-identifiable family: every
finite <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\subseteq L^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\subseteq L^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> lies in a proper sub-language <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> in the collection,
which is exactly the Angluin violation at <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A4.SS2.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="32.78" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 670 32.78" width="670"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,32.78) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><clipPath id="pgfcp25"><path d="M -22670.54 -22670.54 L 22670.54 -22670.54 L 22670.54 22670.54 L -22670.54 22670.54 Z M 0 4.72 L 0 28.06 C 0 30.67 2.12 32.78 4.72 32.78 L 665.28 32.78 C 667.89 32.78 670 30.67 670 28.06 L 670 4.72 C 670 2.12 667.89 0 665.28 0 L 4.72 0 C 2.12 0 0 2.12 0 4.72 Z"></path></clipPath><g fill-rule="evenodd"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F3F7FC;" fill="#F3F7FC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.72 L 0 28.06 C 0 30.67 2.12 32.78 4.72 32.78 L 665.28 32.78 C 667.89 32.78 670 30.67 670 28.06 L 670 4.72 C 670 2.12 667.89 0 665.28 0 L 4.72 0 C 2.12 0 0 2.12 0 4.72 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#6284C2;--ltx-fill-color:#6284C2;--ltx-fg-color:#6284C2;" color="#6284C2" fill="#6284C2" stroke="#6284C2" stroke-width="1.5pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 1.04 32.78 L 1.04 0"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.62 12.93)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:46.45em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="642.74"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A4.SS2.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:46.45em;">
<span id="A4.SS2.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">See <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 3.2 (The exhaustive generator and the separation). ‣ Sound coverage: what the verifier does buy ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(a).</span> Since <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\subseteq F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\subseteq F</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\setminus S_{n}\subseteq F\setminus S_{n}\subseteq F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\setminus S_{n}\subseteq F\setminus S_{n}\subseteq F</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{n}=F\setminus S_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{n}=F\setminus S_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies (<a href="#S2.E6" title="Equation 2.6 ‣ Definition 2.6 (Coverage, soundness, sound coverage). ‣ The nested model: validity versus value ‣ The Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.6</span></a>) at every
round (with <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{*}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{*}=0</annotation></semantics></math>), on every countable pair model, with zero hallucination. When <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\setminus H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\setminus H</annotation></semantics></math> is infinite, the trivia count <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert(F\setminus H)\setminus S_{n}\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert(F\setminus H)\setminus S_{n}\rvert</annotation></semantics></math>
is infinite at every <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(b).</span> Take <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{\dagger}=\{(F_{j},H_{j})\}_{j}\cup\{(F_{\infty},L^{*})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{\dagger}=\{(F_{j},H_{j})\}_{j}\cup\{(F_{\infty},L^{*})\}</annotation></semantics></math> with the
parameters of <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma D.2 (Sandwich-exclusion). ‣ The exhaustive generator and the separation () ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemmas</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a> and <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma D.3 (Fresh-index availability). ‣ The exhaustive generator and the separation () ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a>, choosing the <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{j},A_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{j},A_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> pairwise almost
disjoint (this is a modeling convenience and is not load-bearing: <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma D.2 (Sandwich-exclusion). ‣ The exhaustive generator and the separation () ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a> is
purely column-<math id="A4.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>). All languages are infinite, <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{i}\subsetneq F_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⊊</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{i}\subsetneq F_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}\setminus H_{i}=A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}\setminus H_{i}=A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is infinite.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix any oracle-free set-valued generator <math id="A4.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>. We construct an adversary that defeats it. Fix
the canonical repetition-free enumeration <math id="A4.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A4.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, and maintain the invariant that
after phase <math id="A4.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> the shown set is an initial segment <math id="A4.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{e_{1},\dots,e_{t_{\ell}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{e_{1},\dots,e_{t_{\ell}}\}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A4.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In phase <math id="A4.SS2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, choose (by <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma D.3 (Fresh-index availability). ‣ The exhaustive generator and the separation () ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a>) an index <math id="A4.SS2.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{\ell}&gt;\max(j_{\ell-1},t_{\ell-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{\ell}&gt;\max(j_{\ell-1},t_{\ell-1})</annotation></semantics></math>
with the current shown set contained in <math id="A4.SS2.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{j_{\ell}}\subsetneq L^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo>⊊</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{j_{\ell}}\subsetneq L^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Subphase A.</em><span id="A4.SS2.p8.1.2" class="ltx_text"> Continue the enumeration in <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>-order, but restricted to <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{j_{\ell}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{j_{\ell}}</annotation></semantics></math>
(append not-yet-shown elements of <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{j_{\ell}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{j_{\ell}}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>-order). Two cases.</span></p>
<ul id="A4.I2" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:2.2em;">
<li id="A4.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(A-fail)</em> If <math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> never sound-covers <math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(F_{j_{\ell}},H_{j_{\ell}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(F_{j_{\ell}},H_{j_{\ell}})</annotation></semantics></math> at any
finite round of this continuation, declare <math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(F_{j_{\ell}},H_{j_{\ell}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(F_{j_{\ell}},H_{j_{\ell}})</annotation></semantics></math> the true pair.
The produced sequence is a legal KM enumeration of <math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{j_{\ell}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{j_{\ell}}</annotation></semantics></math>: its initial segment
lies in <math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{j_{\ell}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{j_{\ell}}</annotation></semantics></math> by choice of <math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>j</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the tail exhausts <math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{j_{\ell}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{j_{\ell}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since sound coverage in the limit would in particular hold at some finite round, its
negation means <math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> fails sound coverage at infinitely many rounds, so <math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> fails in the
limit. Done.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(A-succeed)</em> Let <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\prime}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\prime}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> be the first round at which <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{t^{\prime}_{\ell}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{t^{\prime}_{\ell}}</annotation></semantics></math>
sound-covers <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(F_{j_{\ell}},H_{j_{\ell}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(F_{j_{\ell}},H_{j_{\ell}})</annotation></semantics></math>. By <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma D.2 (Sandwich-exclusion). ‣ The exhaustive generator and the separation () ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>, at this round <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>
does <em id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">not</em> sound-cover <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(F_{\infty},L^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(F_{\infty},L^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>.  <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\ddagger)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">‡</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\ddagger)</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Subphase B (only in the (A-succeed) case).</em><span id="A4.SS2.p9.1.2" class="ltx_text"> Let <math id="A4.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> be the maximum <math id="A4.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>-position
among all elements shown through round <math id="A4.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\prime}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\prime}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> (a finite number). Append, in <math id="A4.SS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>-order,
the not-yet-shown elements <math id="A4.SS2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> up to some</span></p>
<table id="A4.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\ell}\ \geq\ \max\bigl(P_{A},\ t_{\ell-1}+1,\ \ell\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\ell}\ \geq\ \max\bigl(P_{A},\ t_{\ell-1}+1,\ \ell\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">restoring the initial-segment invariant: all shown elements lie in <math id="A4.SS2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{e_{1},\dots,e_{t_{\ell}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{e_{1},\dots,e_{t_{\ell}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, repetition-free. The bound (<a href="#A4.E3" title="Equation D.3 ‣ Proof. ‣ The exhaustive generator and the separation () ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a>) clears <math id="A4.SS2.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> because subphase A’s
filtered enumeration may race ahead in <math id="A4.SS2.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>-position.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Conclusion.</em><span id="A4.SS2.p10.1.2" class="ltx_text"> If some phase ends in (A-fail), <math id="A4.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> fails as shown. Otherwise every phase
completes via (A-succeed), so <math id="A4.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\ell}\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\ell}\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> by (<a href="#A4.E3" title="Equation D.3 ‣ Proof. ‣ The exhaustive generator and the separation () ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a>), and the limit sequence
<math id="A4.SS2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math> shows every element of <math id="A4.SS2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> exactly once, a legal KM enumeration of <math id="A4.SS2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. At
each of the infinitely many rounds <math id="A4.SS2.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\prime}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\prime}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS2.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\ddagger)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">‡</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\ddagger)</annotation></semantics></math> holds, so <math id="A4.SS2.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> fails sound coverage
for <math id="A4.SS2.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(F_{\infty},L^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(F_{\infty},L^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> at infinitely many rounds, hence fails in the limit. Declare
<math id="A4.SS2.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(F_{\infty},L^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(F_{\infty},L^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> the true pair. Either way, <math id="A4.SS2.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> fails on <math id="A4.SS2.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(c).</span> Part (a) shows the with-verifier class is all countable pair models; part (b) exhibits a model
outside the without-verifier class. Strictness follows. The breadth contrast is
<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1 (Verification is not taste). ‣ Verification is not taste ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>(c). For the error-relocation reading: under sound coverage all outputs lie in
<math id="A4.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> (no hallucination), and when <math id="A4.SS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\setminus H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\setminus H</annotation></semantics></math> is infinite the trivia count
<math id="A4.SS2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert(F\setminus H)\setminus S_{n}\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert(F\setminus H)\setminus S_{n}\rvert</annotation></semantics></math> is infinite (the exhaustive generator); by
<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1 (Verification is not taste). ‣ Verification is not taste ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>(d) the verifier supplies zero bits about <math id="A4.SS2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> within a fiber, so it cannot
reduce errors or locate value. What it buys is exactly keeping the unavoidable overshoot
inside <math id="A4.SS2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>. The two regimes of part (c) are genuinely distinct: <math id="A4.SS2.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math> has
singleton fibers, so there the verifier identifies the target and <em id="A4.SS2.p11.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">eliminates</em> errors;
the relocation reading is the within-fiber regime.
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#1F4FA8;">The race lemma (<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 3.5 (Race lemma). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>)</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A4.SS3.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="32.78" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 670 32.78" width="670"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,32.78) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><clipPath id="pgfcp26"><path d="M -22670.54 -22670.54 L 22670.54 -22670.54 L 22670.54 22670.54 L -22670.54 22670.54 Z M 0 4.72 L 0 28.06 C 0 30.67 2.12 32.78 4.72 32.78 L 665.28 32.78 C 667.89 32.78 670 30.67 670 28.06 L 670 4.72 C 670 2.12 667.89 0 665.28 0 L 4.72 0 C 2.12 0 0 2.12 0 4.72 Z"></path></clipPath><g fill-rule="evenodd"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F3F7FC;" fill="#F3F7FC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.72 L 0 28.06 C 0 30.67 2.12 32.78 4.72 32.78 L 665.28 32.78 C 667.89 32.78 670 30.67 670 28.06 L 670 4.72 C 670 2.12 667.89 0 665.28 0 L 4.72 0 C 2.12 0 0 2.12 0 4.72 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#6284C2;--ltx-fill-color:#6284C2;--ltx-fg-color:#6284C2;" color="#6284C2" fill="#6284C2" stroke="#6284C2" stroke-width="1.5pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 1.04 32.78 L 1.04 0"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.62 12.93)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:46.45em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="642.74"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A4.SS3.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:46.45em;">
<span id="A4.SS3.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">See <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 3.5 (Race lemma). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Call <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> <em id="A4.SS3.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">resolved at <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math></em> if <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in S_{t}\cup O_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in S_{t}\cup O_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(R1).</span> Let <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> be the first round at which all of <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K[1\!\dots\!M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K[1\!\dots\!M]</annotation></semantics></math> is resolved.</p>
<ol id="A4.I3" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:3.4em;">
<li id="A4.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">Step 1.</span> 
<div id="A4.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At any race round <math id="A4.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in T_{\mathrm{race}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>race</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in T_{\mathrm{race}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K[1\!\dots\!M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K[1\!\dots\!M]</annotation></semantics></math> not yet resolved before
the output, the output is a <em id="A4.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">new</em> element of <math id="A4.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\cap K[1\!\dots\!M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\cap K[1\!\dots\!M]</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed the rule
outputs the <math id="A4.I3.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prec" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≺</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prec</annotation></semantics></math>-least element of <math id="A4.I3.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\setminus(S_{t}\cup O_{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\setminus(S_{t}\cup O_{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math>, and the
<math id="A4.I3.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prec" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≺</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prec</annotation></semantics></math>-least unresolved element of <math id="A4.I3.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> lies in the downward-closed set <math id="A4.I3.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K[1\!\dots\!M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K[1\!\dots\!M]</annotation></semantics></math>
(some element of <math id="A4.I3.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K[1\!\dots\!M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K[1\!\dots\!M]</annotation></semantics></math> is unresolved, and the global minimum over <math id="A4.I3.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> of
unresolved elements is <math id="A4.I3.i1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\preceq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⪯</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\preceq</annotation></semantics></math> it, hence in <math id="A4.I3.i1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K[1\!\dots\!M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K[1\!\dots\!M]</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">Step 2.</span> 
<div id="A4.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consequently <math id="A4.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{M}\leq\tau_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{M}\leq\tau_{M}</annotation></semantics></math>: each of the (at most) <math id="A4.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> race rounds up to <math id="A4.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> that
finds <math id="A4.I3.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K[1\!\dots\!M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K[1\!\dots\!M]</annotation></semantics></math> unresolved contributes a distinct element of <math id="A4.I3.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K[1\!\dots\!M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K[1\!\dots\!M]</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.I3.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>
such contributions exhaust <math id="A4.I3.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K[1\!\dots\!M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K[1\!\dots\!M]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">Step 3.</span> 
<div id="A4.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At most one race round <math id="A4.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq t_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq t_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> is non-contributing: by minimality of <math id="A4.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{M}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A4.I3.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K[1\!\dots\!M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K[1\!\dots\!M]</annotation></semantics></math> is unresolved at every race round strictly before <math id="A4.I3.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, so each such round
contributes; only the round <math id="A4.I3.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> itself may be non-contributing (it may resolve the last
element via the seen-set). Hence <math id="A4.I3.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert O\cap K[1\!\dots\!M]\rvert\geq t_{M}-w(t_{M})-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert O\cap K[1\!\dots\!M]\rvert\geq t_{M}-w(t_{M})-1</annotation></semantics></math>, where
<math id="A4.I3.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(t_{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(t_{M})</annotation></semantics></math> counts the non-race rounds up to <math id="A4.I3.i3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{M}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">Step 4.</span> 
<div id="A4.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Steal bound.</em> Each <math id="A4.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in K[1\!\dots\!M]\setminus O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in K[1\!\dots\!M]\setminus O</annotation></semantics></math> is resolved only by
entering <math id="A4.I3.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t_{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t_{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>; distinct elements have distinct first-enumeration rounds <math id="A4.I3.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq t_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq t_{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A4.I3.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert K[1\!\dots\!M]\setminus O\rvert\leq t_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert K[1\!\dots\!M]\setminus O\rvert\leq t_{M}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Adding Step 3 and Step 4, <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\lvert O\cap K[1\!\dots\!M]\rvert\geq M-w(t_{M})-1\geq M-w(\tau_{M})-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\lvert O\cap K[1\!\dots\!M]\rvert\geq M-w(t_{M})-1\geq M-w(\tau_{M})-1</annotation></semantics></math> (using <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{M}\leq\tau_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{M}\leq\tau_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> and monotonicity of <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>). Since <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{M}=M+w(\tau_{M})\sim M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{M}=M+w(\tau_{M})\sim M</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A4.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=o(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=o(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, dividing by <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> and taking the liminf gives <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{d}(O\cap K,K)\geq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{d}(O\cap K,K)\geq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(R2).</span> <em id="A4.SS3.p4.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Legality of <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>.</em> At <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\neq 2^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\neq 2^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> the adversary enumerates the <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prec" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≺</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prec</annotation></semantics></math>-least element of
<math id="A4.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\setminus(S_{t-1}\cup O_{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\setminus(S_{t-1}\cup O_{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math> (a fresh round); at <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=2^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=2^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> it enumerates the
<math id="A4.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prec" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≺</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prec</annotation></semantics></math>-least element of <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(O_{t-1}\cap K)\setminus S_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∩</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(O_{t-1}\cap K)\setminus S_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> (a recycle round,
draining the generator’s hoarded backlog from the bottom; if empty, it uses the fresh rule as
a fallback). We claim every <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in K</annotation></semantics></math> is enumerated at some finite round, so <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is a legal
repetition-free enumeration of <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>. The <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prec" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≺</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prec</annotation></semantics></math>-least un-enumerated element of <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> advances
monotonically: fresh rounds push it forward, and recycle rounds drain the <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math>-backlog from
the bottom, so no element below the current pointer can be hoarded forever. Hence every fixed
<math id="A4.SS3.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in K</annotation></semantics></math> is enumerated at a finite round. No rate is claimed or needed: legality is eventual
only.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">The cap.</em><span id="A4.SS3.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text"> Fix <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of fresh-enumerated elements in
<math id="A4.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K[1\!\dots\!M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K[1\!\dots\!M]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{M}=O\cap K[1\!\dots\!M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{M}=O\cap K[1\!\dots\!M]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<ol id="A4.I4" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:3.4em;">
<li id="A4.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(C1)</span> 
<div id="A4.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{M}\cap G_{M}=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{M}\cap G_{M}=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> (an element is either enumerated by the adversary or output
by the generator first, in the sense that an output element <math id="A4.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}\notin S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}\notin S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is not
among the fresh-enumerated by definition of the rule), so <math id="A4.I4.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert F_{M}\rvert+\lvert G_{M}\rvert\leq M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert F_{M}\rvert+\lvert G_{M}\rvert\leq M</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(C2)</span> 
<div id="A4.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Injection <math id="A4.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{M}\to F_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{M}\to F_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> up to exceptions.</em> Map the entry round <math id="A4.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> of an
<math id="A4.I4.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math>-element to round <math id="A4.I4.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+1</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A4.I4.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+1</annotation></semantics></math> is a fresh round and <math id="A4.I4.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K[1\!\dots\!M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K[1\!\dots\!M]</annotation></semantics></math> is not yet
fresh-exhausted, the fresh rule at <math id="A4.I4.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+1</annotation></semantics></math> enumerates an element of <math id="A4.I4.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{M}</annotation></semantics></math>. There are exactly
two kinds of exception, which we count separately:</p>
<ol id="A4.I4.i2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:2.4em;">
<li id="A4.I4.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A4.I4.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.I4.i2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">power-of-two recycle rounds:</em> rounds <math id="A4.I4.i2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.I4.i2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+1=2^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+1=2^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Up to the
fresh-exhaustion round <math id="A4.I4.i2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> (defined next) there are at most <math id="A4.I4.i2.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lfloor\log_{2}E_{M}\rfloor+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lfloor\log_{2}E_{M}\rfloor+1</annotation></semantics></math> of these;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I4.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A4.I4.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.I4.i2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">the single post-exhaustion threshold:</em> after <math id="A4.I4.i2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> the fresh rule no longer
enumerates a new element of <math id="A4.I4.i2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K[1\!\dots\!M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K[1\!\dots\!M]</annotation></semantics></math>, costing <math id="A4.I4.i2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1)</annotation></semantics></math> further exceptions.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A4.I4.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Hence the total number of exceptions is at most <math id="A4.I4.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lfloor\log_{2}E_{M}\rfloor+1+O(1)\leq\log_{2}E_{M}+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lfloor\log_{2}E_{M}\rfloor+1+O(1)\leq\log_{2}E_{M}+2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(C3)</span> 
<div id="A4.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">The fresh-exhaustion round <math id="A4.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{M}</annotation></semantics></math>.</em> Define <math id="A4.I4.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> as the round by which every
element of <math id="A4.I4.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K[1\!\dots\!M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K[1\!\dots\!M]</annotation></semantics></math> is used (lies in <math id="A4.I4.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\cup O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\cup O</annotation></semantics></math>), equivalently the round by
which the fresh pointer has passed <math id="A4.I4.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K[M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K[M]</annotation></semantics></math>, skipping any <math id="A4.I4.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math>-hoarded elements. We bound
<math id="A4.I4.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> non-circularly. Each fresh round outputs the <math id="A4.I4.i3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prec" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≺</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prec</annotation></semantics></math>-least un-enumerated element of
<math id="A4.I4.i3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, so fresh claims strictly <math id="A4.I4.i3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prec" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≺</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prec</annotation></semantics></math>-increase the fresh pointer; within <math id="A4.I4.i3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> fresh rounds
the pointer therefore passes <math id="A4.I4.i3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K[M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K[M]</annotation></semantics></math>. Writing <math id="A4.I4.i3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\coloneqq E_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≔</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\coloneqq E_{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, the number of non-fresh
(recycle) rounds up to <math id="A4.I4.i3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is at most <math id="A4.I4.i3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lfloor\log_{2}T\rfloor+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lfloor\log_{2}T\rfloor+1</annotation></semantics></math> (one per power of two
<math id="A4.I4.i3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq T</annotation></semantics></math>), so the number of fresh rounds up to <math id="A4.I4.i3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is at least <math id="A4.I4.i3.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T-\log_{2}T-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T-\log_{2}T-1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Requiring this to reach <math id="A4.I4.i3.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> gives the implicit bound <math id="A4.I4.i3.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\leq M+\log_{2}T+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\leq M+\log_{2}T+1</annotation></semantics></math>; solving it
yields <math id="A4.I4.i3.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{M}\leq M+\log_{2}(M+1)+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{M}\leq M+\log_{2}(M+1)+2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Combining (C1)–(C3): <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert O\cap K[1\!\dots\!M]\rvert=\lvert G_{M}\rvert\leq\lvert F_{M}\rvert+(\log_{2}E_{M}+2)\leq M/2+\log_{2}M+3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert O\cap K[1\!\dots\!M]\rvert=\lvert G_{M}\rvert\leq\lvert F_{M}\rvert+(\log_{2}E_{M}+2)\leq M/2+\log_{2}M+3</annotation></semantics></math>, using <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{M}\leq M+\log_{2}(M+1)+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{M}\leq M+\log_{2}(M+1)+2</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log_{2}E_{M}\leq\log_{2}M+O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log_{2}E_{M}\leq\log_{2}M+O(1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Dividing by <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> and taking the limsup gives <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{d}(O\cap K,K)\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{d}(O\cap K,K)\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Caution on <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{M}</annotation></semantics></math>.</em><span id="A4.SS3.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text"> The round <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> must <em id="A4.SS3.p6.1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">not</em> be read as the round of full
enumeration of <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K[1\!\dots\!M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K[1\!\dots\!M]</annotation></semantics></math>: against a hoarding generator, full enumeration of <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K[1\!\dots\!M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K[1\!\dots\!M]</annotation></semantics></math>
can take exponentially many rounds (the recycle trickle drains the backlog one element per
power-of-two round). The cap argument needs only fresh-exhaustion, which advances at rate <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>
per fresh round.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#1F4FA8;">Impossibility side of the dichotomy (<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 3.6 (Impossibility side of the dichotomy). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a>)</h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A4.SS4.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="32.78" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 670 32.78" width="670"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,32.78) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><clipPath id="pgfcp27"><path d="M -22670.54 -22670.54 L 22670.54 -22670.54 L 22670.54 22670.54 L -22670.54 22670.54 Z M 0 4.72 L 0 28.06 C 0 30.67 2.12 32.78 4.72 32.78 L 665.28 32.78 C 667.89 32.78 670 30.67 670 28.06 L 670 4.72 C 670 2.12 667.89 0 665.28 0 L 4.72 0 C 2.12 0 0 2.12 0 4.72 Z"></path></clipPath><g fill-rule="evenodd"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F3F7FC;" fill="#F3F7FC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.72 L 0 28.06 C 0 30.67 2.12 32.78 4.72 32.78 L 665.28 32.78 C 667.89 32.78 670 30.67 670 28.06 L 670 4.72 C 670 2.12 667.89 0 665.28 0 L 4.72 0 C 2.12 0 0 2.12 0 4.72 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#6284C2;--ltx-fill-color:#6284C2;--ltx-fg-color:#6284C2;" color="#6284C2" fill="#6284C2" stroke="#6284C2" stroke-width="1.5pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 1.04 32.78 L 1.04 0"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.62 12.93)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:46.45em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="642.74"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A4.SS4.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:46.45em;">
<span id="A4.SS4.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">See <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 3.6 (Impossibility side of the dichotomy). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We first record the composition lemma that carries densities between <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.4</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Density composition)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\subseteq K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\subseteq K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> be infinite with <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(K,K^{\prime})=\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(K,K^{\prime})=\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> exact. For any <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subseteq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subseteq K</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{d}(A,K^{\prime})=\alpha\cdot\overline{d}(A,K),\qquad\underline{d}(A,K^{\prime})=\alpha\cdot\underline{d}(A,K)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{d}(A,K^{\prime})=\alpha\cdot\overline{d}(A,K),\qquad\underline{d}(A,K^{\prime})=\alpha\cdot\underline{d}(A,K).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Listings restrict to the canonical order, so <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\cap K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N]=A\cap K[1\!\dots\!m_{N}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\cap K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N]=A\cap K[1\!\dots\!m_{N}]</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="A4.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{N}\coloneqq\lvert K\cap K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N]\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{N}\coloneqq\lvert K\cap K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N]\rvert</annotation></semantics></math>. Write <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{m}\coloneqq\lvert A\cap K[1\!\dots\!m]\rvert/m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{m}\coloneqq\lvert A\cap K[1\!\dots\!m]\rvert/m</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\lvert A\cap K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N]\rvert}{N}=\frac{\lvert A\cap K[1\!\dots\!m_{N}]\rvert}{m_{N}}\cdot\frac{m_{N}}{N}=X_{m_{N}}\cdot\frac{m_{N}}{N}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\lvert A\cap K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N]\rvert}{N}=\frac{\lvert A\cap K[1\!\dots\!m_{N}]\rvert}{m_{N}}\cdot\frac{m_{N}}{N}=X_{m_{N}}\cdot\frac{m_{N}}{N}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">The sequence <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m_{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m_{N})</annotation></semantics></math> is nondecreasing with increments in <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{N}\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{N}\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, so it
hits every large integer; hence <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\limsup_{N}X_{m_{N}}=\limsup_{m}X_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim sup</mo><mi>N</mi></msub><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">lim sup</mo><mi>m</mi></msub><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\limsup_{N}X_{m_{N}}=\limsup_{m}X_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> and likewise for
<math id="A4.SS4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\liminf" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>lim inf</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\liminf</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{N}/N\to\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{N}/N\to\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the limits factor as claimed.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 3.6 (Impossibility side of the dichotomy). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(a).</span> Run any deterministic generator <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> against the racing adversary <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 3.5 (Race lemma). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>(R2).
The transcript is a single object <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math>, and any verifier is fixed advice (<math id="A4.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> under
both readings), so the two readings <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> share it.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Legality of both readings.</em><span id="A4.SS4.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text"> As truth <math id="A4.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is a full repetition-free enumeration of
<math id="A4.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 3.5 (Race lemma). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>(R2)). As truth <math id="A4.SS4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, the same stream is a legal partial enumeration of
<math id="A4.SS4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> with revealed core <math id="A4.SS4.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=K</annotation></semantics></math> of exact density <math id="A4.SS4.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(K,K^{\prime})=\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(K,K^{\prime})=\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>
((<a href="#S3.E2" title="Equation 3.2 ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>)).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Truth <math id="A4.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>.</em><span id="A4.SS4.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text"> By <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 3.5 (Race lemma). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>(R2), <math id="A4.SS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\leq\overline{d}(O\cap K,K)\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\leq\overline{d}(O\cap K,K)\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. coverage <math id="A4.SS4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq 1/2+O(\log M)/M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq 1/2+O(\log M)/M</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.SS4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Truth <math id="A4.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</em><span id="A4.SS4.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text"> Split <math id="A4.SS4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N]=K[1\!\dots\!m_{N}]\sqcup(D\cap K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N]=K[1\!\dots\!m_{N}]\sqcup(D\cap K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N])</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{N}=\lfloor\alpha N\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{N}=\lfloor\alpha N\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math> (by (<a href="#S3.E2" title="Equation 3.2 ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>)). Then</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lvert O\cap K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N]\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lvert O\cap K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N]\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\lvert O\cap K[1\!\dots\!m_{N}]\rvert+\lvert D\cap K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N]\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\lvert O\cap K[1\!\dots\!m_{N}]\rvert+\lvert D\cap K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N]\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\bigl(\tfrac{m_{N}}{2}+\log_{2}m_{N}+3\bigr)+(N-m_{N})=N-\tfrac{m_{N}}{2}+O(\log N)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\bigl(\tfrac{m_{N}}{2}+\log_{2}m_{N}+3\bigr)+(N-m_{N})=N-\tfrac{m_{N}}{2}+O(\log N),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">using <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 3.5 (Race lemma). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>(R2) on the <math id="A4.SS4.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>-part. Dividing by <math id="A4.SS4.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> and taking the liminf gives <math id="A4.SS4.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\leq 1-\alpha/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\leq 1-\alpha/2</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. coverage <math id="A4.SS4.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq 1-\alpha/2+O(\log N)/N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq 1-\alpha/2+O(\log N)/N</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.SS4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Per-instance.</em><span id="A4.SS4.p8.1.2" class="ltx_text"> The caps bind for every generator on the single instance <math id="A4.SS4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>; no
adaptivity to the realized truth is used. Hence no generator guarantees coverage exceeding <math id="A4.SS4.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\alpha/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\alpha/2</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A4.SS4.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, nor exceeding <math id="A4.SS4.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2</annotation></semantics></math> at truth <math id="A4.SS4.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(b).</span> Run <math id="A4.SS4.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> against the same <math id="A4.SS4.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, so the transcript is shared. Suppose <math id="A4.SS4.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> emits finitely many
trivia on every legal instance; in particular at the legal truth-<math id="A4.SS4.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> instance, <math id="A4.SS4.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert O\cap(F\setminus K)\rvert&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert O\cap(F\setminus K)\rvert&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A4.SS4.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}\coloneqq\lvert O\cap D\rvert&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}\coloneqq\lvert O\cap D\rvert&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. At truth <math id="A4.SS4.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert O\cap K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N]\rvert\leq\lvert O\cap K\cap K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N]\rvert+C_{0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert O\cap K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N]\rvert\leq\lvert O\cap K\cap K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N]\rvert+C_{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p9.2" class="ltx_p">Applying <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma D.4 (Density composition). ‣ Impossibility side of the dichotomy () ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a> with <math id="A4.SS4.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=O\cap K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=O\cap K</annotation></semantics></math> and then <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 3.5 (Race lemma). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>(R2),</p>
<table id="A4.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=\underline{d}(O\cap K^{\prime},K^{\prime})\leq\overline{d}(O\cap K,K^{\prime})=\alpha\cdot\overline{d}(O\cap K,K)\leq\alpha\cdot\tfrac{1}{2}=\tfrac{\alpha}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=\underline{d}(O\cap K^{\prime},K^{\prime})\leq\overline{d}(O\cap K,K^{\prime})=\alpha\cdot\overline{d}(O\cap K,K)\leq\alpha\cdot\tfrac{1}{2}=\tfrac{\alpha}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(c).</span> The contrapositive of (b): any generator guaranteeing coverage exceeding <math id="A4.SS4.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha/2</annotation></semantics></math> on all of
<math id="A4.SS4.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> must emit infinitely many trivia on some instance. Exactness of the finite-trivia
frontier at <math id="A4.SS4.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha/2</annotation></semantics></math> follows from <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem7" title="Theorem 3.7 (Achievability side: sweep and the tight generator). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.7</span></a>(iii), which attains <math id="A4.SS4.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha/2</annotation></semantics></math> at truth
<math id="A4.SS4.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> with eventually zero trivia.
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#1F4FA8;">Achievability: sweep and the tight generator (<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem7" title="Theorem 3.7 (Achievability side: sweep and the tight generator). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.7</span></a>)</h3>

<div id="A4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A4.SS5.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="32.78" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 670 32.78" width="670"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,32.78) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><clipPath id="pgfcp28"><path d="M -22670.54 -22670.54 L 22670.54 -22670.54 L 22670.54 22670.54 L -22670.54 22670.54 Z M 0 4.72 L 0 28.06 C 0 30.67 2.12 32.78 4.72 32.78 L 665.28 32.78 C 667.89 32.78 670 30.67 670 28.06 L 670 4.72 C 670 2.12 667.89 0 665.28 0 L 4.72 0 C 2.12 0 0 2.12 0 4.72 Z"></path></clipPath><g fill-rule="evenodd"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F3F7FC;" fill="#F3F7FC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.72 L 0 28.06 C 0 30.67 2.12 32.78 4.72 32.78 L 665.28 32.78 C 667.89 32.78 670 30.67 670 28.06 L 670 4.72 C 670 2.12 667.89 0 665.28 0 L 4.72 0 C 2.12 0 0 2.12 0 4.72 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#6284C2;--ltx-fill-color:#6284C2;--ltx-fg-color:#6284C2;" color="#6284C2" fill="#6284C2" stroke="#6284C2" stroke-width="1.5pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 1.04 32.78 L 1.04 0"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.62 12.93)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:46.45em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="642.74"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A4.SS5.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:46.45em;">
<span id="A4.SS5.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">See <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem7" title="Theorem 3.7 (Achievability side: sweep and the tight generator). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.7</span></a></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pointer lemma.</span> We first prove the fact that drives both generators.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.5</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Pointer lemma)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose at each sweep round <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in R</annotation></semantics></math> the generator outputs the <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prec" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≺</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prec</annotation></semantics></math>-least element of <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{t}\setminus(S_{t}\cup O_{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{t}\setminus(S_{t}\cup O_{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math> for a family <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\subseteq V_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\subseteq V_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>,
and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is infinite. Then for every <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in H</annotation></semantics></math> never enumerated by the adversary, <math id="A4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in O</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix such an <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>-position <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\subseteq V_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\subseteq V_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> always, <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in V_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in V_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>; since
<math id="A4.SS5.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is never enumerated, <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\notin S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\notin S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\notin O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\notin O</annotation></semantics></math>. At every
sweep round <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in R</annotation></semantics></math>, the output is the <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prec" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≺</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prec</annotation></semantics></math>-least element of <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{t}\setminus(S_{t}\cup O_{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{t}\setminus(S_{t}\cup O_{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math>, which is <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\preceq x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⪯</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\preceq x</annotation></semantics></math> (as <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> itself is available) and <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\neq x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≠</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\neq x</annotation></semantics></math> (as <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\notin O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\notin O</annotation></semantics></math>), hence strictly <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prec x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≺</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prec x</annotation></semantics></math> — a new element of <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> strictly below position <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>. But
only <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p-1</annotation></semantics></math> positions lie below <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is infinite, a contradiction. Hence <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in O</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">(i) Universal sweep <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\mathrm{sw}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>sw</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\mathrm{sw}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{t}=\bigcup\{H^{\prime}\in\mathcal{H}:S_{t}\subseteq H^{\prime}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⋃</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{t}=\bigcup\{H^{\prime}\in\mathcal{H}:S_{t}\subseteq H^{\prime}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and the sweep schedule <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=\{k^{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=\{k^{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Apply <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma D.5 (Pointer lemma). ‣ Proof. ‣ Achievability: sweep and the tight generator () ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.5</span></a> with <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{t}=U_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{t}=U_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>: for any <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in H\setminus C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in H\setminus C</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is consistent (<math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}\subseteq C\subseteq H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}\subseteq C\subseteq H</annotation></semantics></math>) so <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\in\mathcal{H}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\in\mathcal{H}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in U_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in U_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, while <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\notin C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\notin C</annotation></semantics></math> is never enumerated. Hence <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\supseteq H\setminus C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⊇</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\supseteq H\setminus C</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore</p>
<table id="A4.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert O\cap H[1\!\dots\!N]\rvert\geq N-\lvert C\cap H[1\!\dots\!N]\rvert,\qquad\text{so}\qquad c\geq 1-\overline{d}(C,H)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mtext>so</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert O\cap H[1\!\dots\!N]\rvert\geq N-\lvert C\cap H[1\!\dots\!N]\rvert,\qquad\text{so}\qquad c\geq 1-\overline{d}(C,H),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which is <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 1-\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 1-\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(C,H)=\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(C,H)=\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> exists. <em id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Trivia rate.</em> By
<a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Fact 2.2 (Chain validity in the partial model; ( , , Lemma 2.5(1) in arXiv version)). ‣ Partial enumeration and the revealed core ‣ The Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fact</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a> there is a finite <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}^{(t)}\subseteq H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>⊆</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}^{(t)}\subseteq H</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq T_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq T_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, so every non-sweep output from <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> on lies in <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>; the only possible trivia rounds
among <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[1\dots N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[1\dots N]</annotation></semantics></math> are the <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq T_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq T_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> early non-sweep rounds and the <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lfloor\sqrt{N}\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lfloor\sqrt{N}\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>
sweep rounds, giving a trivia count <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq T_{0}+\lfloor\sqrt{N}\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq T_{0}+\lfloor\sqrt{N}\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math> and rate <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>. The
count is infinite in general, necessarily so, by <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 3.6 (Impossibility side of the dichotomy). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a>(c). <em id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Soundness.</em> <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{t}\subseteq\bigcup\mathcal{H}\subseteq F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">⊆</mo><mrow><mo>⋃</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{t}\subseteq\bigcup\mathcal{H}\subseteq F</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in some candidate
<math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\subseteq F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⊆</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\subseteq F</annotation></semantics></math>; the fallback lies in <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\subseteq F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\subseteq F</annotation></semantics></math>: zero
hallucination.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">(The restated KW lemma is used only for the non-sweep half of the trivia bound. A bare
conjunction default would fail on a general <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>: for <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}=\{\mathbb{N}\setminus\{n\}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}=\{\mathbb{N}\setminus\{n\}\}</annotation></semantics></math> the
conjunction of consistent candidates is just <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. On <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> below avoids this
restated lemma entirely.)</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(ii) Tight generator <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> Recall <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{t}=\{H^{\prime}\in\mathcal{H}_{\alpha}:S_{t}\subseteq H^{\prime}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{t}=\{H^{\prime}\in\mathcal{H}_{\alpha}:S_{t}\subseteq H^{\prime}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{t}=\bigcap\mathcal{H}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>⋂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{t}=\bigcap\mathcal{H}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{t}=\bigcup\mathcal{H}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>⋃</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{t}=\bigcup\mathcal{H}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. The structure is:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}\subseteq K\ \Longrightarrow\ \mathcal{H}_{t}=\{K,K^{\prime}\},\ I_{t}=K,\ U_{t}=K^{\prime};\qquad S_{t}\not\subseteq K\ \Longrightarrow\ \mathcal{H}_{t}=\{K^{\prime}\},\ I_{t}=U_{t}=K^{\prime}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⊈</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}\subseteq K\ \Longrightarrow\ \mathcal{H}_{t}=\{K,K^{\prime}\},\ I_{t}=K,\ U_{t}=K^{\prime};\qquad S_{t}\not\subseteq K\ \Longrightarrow\ \mathcal{H}_{t}=\{K^{\prime}\},\ I_{t}=U_{t}=K^{\prime}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(a) Truth <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>.</em> Here every enumerated element is in <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subseteq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subseteq K</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}\subseteq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}\subseteq K</annotation></semantics></math> always and <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{t}=K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{t}=K</annotation></semantics></math>. The non-sweep rounds form the set <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{N}\setminus R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{N}\setminus R</annotation></semantics></math>, of
density <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(t)=\lfloor\sqrt{t}\rfloor=o(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(t)=\lfloor\sqrt{t}\rfloor=o(t)</annotation></semantics></math>; on them <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> runs
<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 3.5 (Race lemma). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>(R1)’s greedy race on <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> (the <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prec" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≺</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prec</annotation></semantics></math>-least element of <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{t}\setminus(S_{t}\cup O_{t-1})=K\setminus(S_{t}\cup O_{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{t}\setminus(S_{t}\cup O_{t-1})=K\setminus(S_{t}\cup O_{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math>). Thus <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{d}(O\cap K,K)\geq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{d}(O\cap K,K)\geq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\geq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\geq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma D.5 (Pointer lemma). ‣ Proof. ‣ Achievability: sweep and the tight generator () ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.5</span></a> with <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{t}=U_{t}=K^{\prime}\supseteq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⊇</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{t}=U_{t}=K^{\prime}\supseteq K</annotation></semantics></math>
gives <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\supseteq K\setminus C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⊇</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\supseteq K\setminus C</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\geq 1-\overline{d}(C,K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\geq 1-\overline{d}(C,K)</annotation></semantics></math>; together <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\geq\max(1/2,1-\overline{d}(C,K))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\geq\max(1/2,1-\overline{d}(C,K))</annotation></semantics></math>. <em id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Trivia.</em> Race outputs lie in <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>; the sweep covers <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{t}=K^{\prime}\supseteq D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⊇</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{t}=K^{\prime}\supseteq D</annotation></semantics></math>, so trivia rounds among <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[1\dots N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[1\dots N]</annotation></semantics></math> number <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq\lfloor\sqrt{N}\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq\lfloor\sqrt{N}\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>,
rate <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Note <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\cap D=D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\cap D=D</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">infinite</em>: the sweep eventually claims all of
<math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> via <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma D.5 (Pointer lemma). ‣ Proof. ‣ Achievability: sweep and the tight generator () ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.5</span></a> (each <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\in D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\in D</annotation></semantics></math> lies in <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{t}=K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{t}=K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and is never enumerated at truth
<math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>). This infinitude is exactly why <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 3.6 (Impossibility side of the dichotomy). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a>(b)’s finite-trivia cap does not apply to
<math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(b) Truth <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subseteq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subseteq K</annotation></semantics></math>.</em> The transcript is identical to case (a):
<math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subseteq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subseteq K</annotation></semantics></math> means <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}\subseteq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}\subseteq K</annotation></semantics></math> throughout, so <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> cannot and need not
distinguish the two truths, and runs (R1)’s race on <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> exactly as before. By
<a href="#A4.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma D.5 (Pointer lemma). ‣ Proof. ‣ Achievability: sweep and the tight generator () ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.5</span></a> with <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> (every <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in K^{\prime}\setminus C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∖</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in K^{\prime}\setminus C</annotation></semantics></math> is never enumerated and
lies in <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{t}=K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{t}=K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>), <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\supseteq K^{\prime}\setminus C\supseteq D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⊇</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∖</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>⊇</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\supseteq K^{\prime}\setminus C\supseteq D</annotation></semantics></math>. For coverage, split
<math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N]=K[1\!\dots\!m_{N}]\sqcup(D\cap K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N]=K[1\!\dots\!m_{N}]\sqcup(D\cap K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N])</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{N}=\lfloor\alpha N\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{N}=\lfloor\alpha N\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>); the sweep claims all <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N-m_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N-m_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> elements of <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\cap K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\cap K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N]</annotation></semantics></math> and the race
claims at least <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{N}/2-O(\sqrt{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{N}/2-O(\sqrt{N})</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K[1\!\dots\!m_{N}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K[1\!\dots\!m_{N}]</annotation></semantics></math>, and the two parts are disjoint, so</p>
<table id="A4.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert O\cap K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N]\rvert\geq(N-m_{N})+\tfrac{m_{N}}{2}-O(\sqrt{N})=N\bigl(1-\tfrac{\alpha}{2}\bigr)-O(\sqrt{N})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert O\cap K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N]\rvert\geq(N-m_{N})+\tfrac{m_{N}}{2}-O(\sqrt{N})=N\bigl(1-\tfrac{\alpha}{2}\bigr)-O(\sqrt{N}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">giving <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\geq 1-\alpha/2-o(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\geq 1-\alpha/2-o(1)</annotation></semantics></math>. <em id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Trivia.</em> Race outputs <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\subseteq K\subseteq K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⊆</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\subseteq K\subseteq K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>
and sweep outputs <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\subseteq K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\subseteq K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <em id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">zero</em> trivia at truth <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(c) Truth <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\not\subseteq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\not\subseteq K</annotation></semantics></math>.</em> Let <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> be the first (finite) round with
<math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t_{0}}\notin K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>∉</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t_{0}}\notin K</annotation></semantics></math>. From <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> on, <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}\not\subseteq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⊈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}\not\subseteq K</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{t}=U_{t}=K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{t}=U_{t}=K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Apply
<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 3.5 (Race lemma). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>(R1) with <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\leftarrow K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\leftarrow K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mathrm{race}}=(\mathbb{N}\setminus R)\setminus[1\dots t_{0}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>race</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mathrm{race}}=(\mathbb{N}\setminus R)\setminus[1\dots t_{0}]</annotation></semantics></math> (still density <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>): <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\geq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\geq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>. <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma D.5 (Pointer lemma). ‣ Proof. ‣ Achievability: sweep and the tight generator () ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.5</span></a> with <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{t}=U_{t}=K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{t}=U_{t}=K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>
gives <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\geq 1-\overline{d}(C,K^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\geq 1-\overline{d}(C,K^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>; together <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\geq\max(1/2,1-\overline{d}(C,K^{\prime}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\geq\max(1/2,1-\overline{d}(C,K^{\prime}))</annotation></semantics></math>. All
outputs lie in <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, so zero trivia.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Scope.</em> The unqualified “<math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\alpha/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\alpha/2</annotation></semantics></math> at truth <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>” is false for general <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subseteq K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subseteq K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>: if <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> enumerated by the racing adversary, the cap of
<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 3.5 (Race lemma). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>(R2) holds with <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\leftarrow K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\leftarrow K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and pins every generator at <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2</annotation></semantics></math>. Case (b)’s
restriction <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subseteq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subseteq K</annotation></semantics></math> is exactly the regime the dichotomy needs.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(iii) Finite-trivia side (restated).</span> By <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Fact 2.1 (Partial-enumeration generation; ( , , Theorem 1.6 in arXiv version)). ‣ Partial enumeration and the revealed core ‣ The Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fact</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>, KW’s generator achieves <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{d}(O,H)\geq\tfrac{1}{2}\underline{d}(C,H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>O</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{d}(O,H)\geq\tfrac{1}{2}\underline{d}(C,H)</annotation></semantics></math> for every countable collection, never consulting <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>; generation in the
limit gives <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exists t^{*}\,\forall t\geq t^{*}:a_{t}\in H\setminus S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exists t^{*}\,\forall t\geq t^{*}:a_{t}\in H\setminus S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, so the trivia
rounds are confined to <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&lt;t^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&lt;t^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>: eventually zero. Because <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\subseteq F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\subseteq F</annotation></semantics></math>, the same
statement <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}\in H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}\in H</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq t^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq t^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> makes the generator <em id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">eventually sound</em> (<math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}\in F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}\in F</annotation></semantics></math>) as well; this is exactly what our model’s soundness (eventually <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}\in F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}\in F</annotation></semantics></math>) and
finite-trivia (eventually <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}\notin F\setminus H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}\notin F\setminus H</annotation></semantics></math>) hypotheses require, and it follows
from the generation guarantee alone. No claim about the pre-<math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> outputs (and in particular
no inference from the internal pod construction of KW’s generator) is needed for the
load-bearing path. On <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> this yields <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha/2</annotation></semantics></math> at truth <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2</annotation></semantics></math> at truth <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>,
matching the caps of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 3.6 (Impossibility side of the dichotomy). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark D.6</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(Non-load-bearing aside)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">KW’s pods are in fact candidate-contained at all times, so one expects the pre-<math id="A4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> outputs
also to lie in <math id="A4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> here; we record this only as an aside, as the eventual-soundness
argument above already supplies everything the dichotomy uses.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#1F4FA8;">The instantiation (<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1 (Abelian refinement chains are identifiable). ‣ Case Study: Instantiation in a Compression Model of Mathematics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorems</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 4.2 (Free-monoid pairs realize the dichotomy). ‣ Case Study: Instantiation in a Compression Model of Mathematics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> and <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 4.3 (Imprecision of exhaustive generation). ‣ Case Study: Instantiation in a Compression Model of Mathematics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>)</h3>

<section id="A4.SS6.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#1F4FA8;">Abelian refinement chains (<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1 (Abelian refinement chains are identifiable). ‣ Case Study: Instantiation in a Compression Model of Mathematics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>)</h4>

<div id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="32.78" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 670 32.78" width="670"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,32.78) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><clipPath id="pgfcp29"><path d="M -22670.54 -22670.54 L 22670.54 -22670.54 L 22670.54 22670.54 L -22670.54 22670.54 Z M 0 4.72 L 0 28.06 C 0 30.67 2.12 32.78 4.72 32.78 L 665.28 32.78 C 667.89 32.78 670 30.67 670 28.06 L 670 4.72 C 670 2.12 667.89 0 665.28 0 L 4.72 0 C 2.12 0 0 2.12 0 4.72 Z"></path></clipPath><g fill-rule="evenodd"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F3F7FC;" fill="#F3F7FC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.72 L 0 28.06 C 0 30.67 2.12 32.78 4.72 32.78 L 665.28 32.78 C 667.89 32.78 670 30.67 670 28.06 L 670 4.72 C 670 2.12 667.89 0 665.28 0 L 4.72 0 C 2.12 0 0 2.12 0 4.72 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#6284C2;--ltx-fill-color:#6284C2;--ltx-fg-color:#6284C2;" color="#6284C2" fill="#6284C2" stroke="#6284C2" stroke-width="1.5pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 1.04 32.78 L 1.04 0"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.62 12.93)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:46.45em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="642.74"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:46.45em;">
<span id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">See <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1 (Abelian refinement chains are identifiable). ‣ Case Study: Instantiation in a Compression Model of Mathematics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Write <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=\prod_{i}a_{i}^{N_{i}}\in A_{n}\cong(\mathbb{N}^{n},+)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℕ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=\prod_{i}a_{i}^{N_{i}}\in A_{n}\cong(\mathbb{N}^{n},+)</annotation></semantics></math>, identified with its exponent vector
<math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(N_{1},\dots,N_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(N_{1},\dots,N_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>. We use three lemmas.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.7</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Digit-sum formula)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For the geometric dictionary <math id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{c}=\{c^{\,j}a_{i}:i\leq n,j\geq 1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{c}=\{c^{\,j}a_{i}:i\leq n,j\geq 1\}</annotation></semantics></math> (with <math id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=b_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=b_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>),
the wrapped length is <math id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert w\rvert_{G\cup D_{c}}=\sum_{i=1}^{n}s_{c}(N_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert w\rvert_{G\cup D_{c}}=\sum_{i=1}^{n}s_{c}(N_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{c}(N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{c}(N)</annotation></semantics></math> is the
sum of the base-<math id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> digits of <math id="A4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.SSS1.2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Each coordinate <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}^{N_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}^{N_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> is factored independently (the dictionary words are single-letter
powers). For one coordinate: a factoring corresponds to a representation of <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> as a sum of
powers of <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> with nonnegative integer coefficients (multiplicities), and its symbol count is
the sum of those multiplicities. Replacing <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> copies of the macro <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\,j}a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\,j}a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> by one copy
of <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\,j+1}a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\,j+1}a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> preserves the represented power and strictly decreases the symbol count, so
every minimizing representation has all multiplicities <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;c</annotation></semantics></math>; the unique representation with
all multiplicities <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;c</annotation></semantics></math> is the base-<math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> representation of <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence the minimum symbol
count is its digit sum <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{c}(N_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{c}(N_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. Summing over coordinates gives the formula.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.8</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Nesting)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{D_{t+1}}\subseteq H_{D_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{D_{t+1}}\subseteq H_{D_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, so <math id="A4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{H_{D_{t}}\}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{H_{D_{t}}\}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is a descending chain.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.SSS1.2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t+1}=b_{t}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t+1}=b_{t}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{t+1}\subseteq D_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{t+1}\subseteq D_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. A richer dictionary cannot increase
the minimal factoring length, so <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert w\rvert_{G\cup D_{t}}\leq\lvert w\rvert_{G\cup D_{t+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert w\rvert_{G\cup D_{t}}\leq\lvert w\rvert_{G\cup D_{t+1}}</annotation></semantics></math> for every
<math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore every <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert w\rvert_{G\cup D_{t+1}}\leq\theta_{\kappa}(\lvert w\rvert_{G})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert w\rvert_{G\cup D_{t+1}}\leq\theta_{\kappa}(\lvert w\rvert_{G})</annotation></semantics></math> also
satisfies <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert w\rvert_{G\cup D_{t}}\leq\theta_{\kappa}(\lvert w\rvert_{G})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert w\rvert_{G\cup D_{t}}\leq\theta_{\kappa}(\lvert w\rvert_{G})</annotation></semantics></math>: membership transfers downward
and the chain is descending.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.9</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Witness / singleton tell-tale)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}\coloneqq a_{1}^{\,b_{t}+b_{t}^{3}}\in H_{D_{t}}\setminus H_{D_{t+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}\coloneqq a_{1}^{\,b_{t}+b_{t}^{3}}\in H_{D_{t}}\setminus H_{D_{t+1}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{t}=\{w_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{t}=\{w_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math>
is a tell-tale for <math id="A4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{D_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{D_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> in the chain.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.SSS1.2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">By <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem7" title="Lemma D.7 (Digit-sum formula). ‣ Proof. ‣ Abelian refinement chains () ‣ The instantiation (, and ) ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.7</span></a>, <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert w_{t}\rvert_{G\cup D_{t}}=s_{b_{t}}(b_{t}+b_{t}^{3})=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert w_{t}\rvert_{G\cup D_{t}}=s_{b_{t}}(b_{t}+b_{t}^{3})=2</annotation></semantics></math> (the number <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t}+b_{t}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t}+b_{t}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math> has base-<math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> digits <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> at positions <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>). In base <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t+1}=b_{t}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t+1}=b_{t}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the
same number is <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t}+b_{t}\cdot b_{t}^{2}=b_{t}(1+b_{t}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t}+b_{t}\cdot b_{t}^{2}=b_{t}(1+b_{t}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, whose base-<math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> digit sum is <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2b_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2b_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> (a digit <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> at positions <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>). The raw length is <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert w_{t}\rvert_{G}=b_{t}+b_{t}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert w_{t}\rvert_{G}=b_{t}+b_{t}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>,
so <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\kappa}(\lvert w_{t}\rvert_{G})=\kappa\log_{2}(1+b_{t}+b_{t}^{3})\leq 5\kappa\log_{2}b_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\kappa}(\lvert w_{t}\rvert_{G})=\kappa\log_{2}(1+b_{t}+b_{t}^{3})\leq 5\kappa\log_{2}b_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> for
large <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert w_{t}\rvert_{G\cup D_{t}}=2\leq\theta_{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert w_{t}\rvert_{G\cup D_{t}}=2\leq\theta_{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}\in H_{D_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}\in H_{D_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>;
while <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert w_{t}\rvert_{G\cup D_{t+1}}=2b_{t}&gt;5\kappa\log_{2}b_{t}\geq\theta_{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert w_{t}\rvert_{G\cup D_{t+1}}=2b_{t}&gt;5\kappa\log_{2}b_{t}\geq\theta_{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\geq 16\kappa^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\geq 16\kappa^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> forces <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2b_{t}&gt;5\kappa\log_{2}b_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2b_{t}&gt;5\kappa\log_{2}b_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}\notin H_{D_{t+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}\notin H_{D_{t+1}}</annotation></semantics></math>. As the chain
is descending, <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{w_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{w_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math> separates <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{D_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{D_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> from every proper sub-language
<math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{D_{t^{\prime}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{D_{t^{\prime}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\prime}&gt;t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\prime}&gt;t</annotation></semantics></math>: any <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{D_{t^{\prime}}}\ni w_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></msub><mo>∋</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{D_{t^{\prime}}}\ni w_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> would need <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\prime}\leq t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\prime}\leq t</annotation></semantics></math>, so no proper
sub-language contains the tell-tale. The languages are infinite (e.g. all <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}^{c^{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}^{c^{j}}</annotation></semantics></math> have
wrapped length <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p5.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">The three lemmas give a strictly descending chain of infinite languages with singleton
tell-tales, so <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{\mathrm{ab}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>ab</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{\mathrm{ab}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies Angluin’s condition. By <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1 (Verification is not taste). ‣ Verification is not taste ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>(a),
applied in the single fiber <math id="A4.SS6.SSS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=A_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=A_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, exact breadth in the limit is achievable: in the
abelian regime valuable generation needs no trivia. (The partial-enumeration behavior of the
chain, its relative densities, is open.)
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS6.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#1F4FA8;">Free-monoid pairs (<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 4.2 (Free-monoid pairs realize the dichotomy). ‣ Case Study: Instantiation in a Compression Model of Mathematics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>)</h4>

<div id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="32.78" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 670 32.78" width="670"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,32.78) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><clipPath id="pgfcp30"><path d="M -22670.54 -22670.54 L 22670.54 -22670.54 L 22670.54 22670.54 L -22670.54 22670.54 Z M 0 4.72 L 0 28.06 C 0 30.67 2.12 32.78 4.72 32.78 L 665.28 32.78 C 667.89 32.78 670 30.67 670 28.06 L 670 4.72 C 670 2.12 667.89 0 665.28 0 L 4.72 0 C 2.12 0 0 2.12 0 4.72 Z"></path></clipPath><g fill-rule="evenodd"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F3F7FC;" fill="#F3F7FC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.72 L 0 28.06 C 0 30.67 2.12 32.78 4.72 32.78 L 665.28 32.78 C 667.89 32.78 670 30.67 670 28.06 L 670 4.72 C 670 2.12 667.89 0 665.28 0 L 4.72 0 C 2.12 0 0 2.12 0 4.72 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#6284C2;--ltx-fill-color:#6284C2;--ltx-fg-color:#6284C2;" color="#6284C2" fill="#6284C2" stroke="#6284C2" stroke-width="1.5pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 1.04 32.78 L 1.04 0"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.62 12.93)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:46.45em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="642.74"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:46.45em;">
<span id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">See <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 4.2 (Free-monoid pairs realize the dichotomy). ‣ Case Study: Instantiation in a Compression Model of Mathematics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.SSS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(i) Name-cut pairs.</span> With the bounded cut <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\equiv 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\equiv 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the compressible language is exactly the nameable
corpus <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{D,1}=G\cup D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{D,1}=G\cup D</annotation></semantics></math>: the letters <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{a,x\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{a,x\}</annotation></semantics></math> together with the macro words. Each
<math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{m,i}=x^{i}a\,x^{q+1-i}a\,x^{2^{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></msup></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{m,i}=x^{i}a\,x^{q+1-i}a\,x^{2^{m}}</annotation></semantics></math> has a <em id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">unique</em> parsing (the two <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>’s mark
the boundaries, and the three <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>-blocks have lengths <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q+1-i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q+1-i</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> recovering <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m,i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m,i</annotation></semantics></math>
unambiguously), so the words are distinct and the <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>-position encodes <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Order <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> by
length-then-lex. For each <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> words <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mu_{m,i}\}_{i=1}^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>q</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mu_{m,i}\}_{i=1}^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> form an equal-length
stratum (all have length <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q+3+2^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q+3+2^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>), lex-ordered by <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> via the position of the first <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>.
Of these <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> words, the <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\leq p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\leq p</annotation></semantics></math> lie in <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>; so within each stratum the count of
<math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>-elements is <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> out of <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>. Summing over strata up to position <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert K\cap K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N]\rvert=\alpha N+O(q),\qquad\alpha=p/q," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert K\cap K^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N]\rvert=\alpha N+O(q),\qquad\alpha=p/q,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">the <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(q)</annotation></semantics></math> accounting for the partial last stratum and the two letters. Hence <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(K,K^{\prime})=\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(K,K^{\prime})=\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> exactly. The pair <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(K,K^{\prime},F_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(K,K^{\prime},F_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> meets the interface of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem11" title="Remark 3.11 (Interface of the impossibility proofs). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Remark</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.11</span></a>: <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is
countable with the length-then-lex canonical order; <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\subsetneq K^{\prime}\subseteq F_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⊊</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\subsetneq K^{\prime}\subseteq F_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are
infinite; <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{n}\setminus K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{n}\setminus K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is infinite (it contains all non-macro words); and <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p2.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{N}=\alpha N+O(q)=\alpha N+O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{N}=\alpha N+O(q)=\alpha N+O(1)</annotation></semantics></math>. By <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem11" title="Remark 3.11 (Interface of the impossibility proofs). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Remark</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.11</span></a>, <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 3.5 (Race lemma). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemmas</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a> and <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 3.6 (Impossibility side of the dichotomy). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a> hold verbatim
for this pair, so the dichotomy (<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem10" title="Corollary 3.10 (The trivia dichotomy). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Corollary</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.10</span></a>) holds inside the compression model.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(ii) Obstruction.</span> Now use the unbounded cut <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> with dictionary-only wrapped length and the nested
tag-dictionaries built from <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{m,i}=aa\,x^{i}a\,x^{q+1-i}a\,x^{2^{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></msup></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{m,i}=aa\,x^{i}a\,x^{q+1-i}a\,x^{2^{m}}</annotation></semantics></math> (the leading
<math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="aa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">aa</annotation></semantics></math>-block is a unique delimiter). Parsing is unique via the <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="aa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">aa</annotation></semantics></math>-blocks. Write <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(L)</annotation></semantics></math> for the number of compressible strings of length <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq L</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{k}(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{k}(L)</annotation></semantics></math> for those parsing
into exactly <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> tag-blocks (<math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>). We bound the upper density <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{d}(\hat{K},\hat{K}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{d}(\hat{K},\hat{K}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> in
five displayed steps.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(1) Deletion injection.</em><span id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text"> Map a <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-block word (<math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>) to the <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k-1)</annotation></semantics></math>-block word
obtained by deleting its first <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="aa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">aa</annotation></semantics></math>-block (and the empty word for <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math>). A preimage of a
given image is recovered by choosing the deleted block: a tag <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[q]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[q]</annotation></semantics></math> and a scale <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\leq\log_{2}L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\leq\log_{2}L</annotation></semantics></math>, so each image has at most <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+q(\log_{2}L+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+q(\log_{2}L+1)</annotation></semantics></math> preimages. Hence</span></p>
<table id="A4.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(L)\ \leq\ \bigl(1+q+q\log_{2}L\bigr)\,\mathcal{N}(L-1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(L)\ \leq\ \bigl(1+q+q\log_{2}L\bigr)\,\mathcal{N}(L-1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(2) Small-<math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> mass.</em><span id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text"> A length-<math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq L</annotation></semantics></math> word with <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> blocks chooses, per block, a tag <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\leq q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\leq q</annotation></semantics></math> and a scale <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{m}\leq L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{m}\leq L</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e. <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\leq\log_{2}L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\leq\log_{2}L</annotation></semantics></math>), so <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{k}(L)\leq q^{k}(\log_{2}L+1)^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{k}(L)\leq q^{k}(\log_{2}L+1)^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\coloneqq\lceil 2\log\log L/\log(q/p)\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\coloneqq\lceil 2\log\log L/\log(q/p)\rceil</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k\leq B}N_{k}(L)\ \leq\ B\,q^{B}(\log_{2}L+1)^{B}\ =\ \exp\!\bigl(O((\log\log L)^{2})\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>B</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>B</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k\leq B}N_{k}(L)\ \leq\ B\,q^{B}(\log_{2}L+1)^{B}\ =\ \exp\!\bigl(O((\log\log L)^{2})\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(3) Tag truncation.</em><span id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text"> A <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-block word lies in <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{K}</annotation></semantics></math> only if all <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> tags satisfy <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\leq p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\leq p</annotation></semantics></math> (versus all <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\leq q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\leq q</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{K}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{K}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>). For <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;B</annotation></semantics></math> this costs a factor at most</span></p>
<table id="A4.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p/q)^{k}\ \leq\ (p/q)^{B}\ =\ (\log L)^{-2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>B</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p/q)^{k}\ \leq\ (p/q)^{B}\ =\ (\log L)^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">on the corresponding mass, by the choice of <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(4) Lower bound on <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.</em><span id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text"> The true count is exponential in <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>; we need only the
weaker</span></p>
<table id="A4.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(L)\ \geq\ \exp\!\bigl(c\,\log L\cdot\log\log L\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(L)\ \geq\ \exp\!\bigl(c\,\log L\cdot\log\log L\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">witnessed at the block count <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{*}=\lfloor\kappa\log_{2}(1+\sqrt{L})\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>L</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{*}=\lfloor\kappa\log_{2}(1+\sqrt{L})\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>: force one
scale near <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>L</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{L}</annotation></semantics></math> so every word passes the cut <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math>, and choose the remaining
<math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{*}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{*}-1</annotation></semantics></math> scales freely below <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{L}/k^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>L</mi></msqrt><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{L}/k^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. This weaker bound suffices.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(5) Conclusion.</em><span id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p8.1.2" class="ltx_text"> Split the <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{K}</annotation></semantics></math>-mass at <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> blocks. By (<a href="#A4.E5" title="Equation D.5 ‣ Proof. ‣ Free-monoid pairs () ‣ The instantiation (, and ) ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.5</span></a>) the <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leq B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leq B</annotation></semantics></math> part is <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(O((\log\log L)^{2}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(O((\log\log L)^{2}))</annotation></semantics></math>; by (<a href="#A4.E6" title="Equation D.6 ‣ Proof. ‣ Free-monoid pairs () ‣ The instantiation (, and ) ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.6</span></a>) the <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;B</annotation></semantics></math> part is at most
<math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\log L)^{-2}\,\mathcal{N}(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\log L)^{-2}\,\mathcal{N}(L)</annotation></semantics></math>. With (<a href="#A4.E4" title="Equation D.4 ‣ Proof. ‣ Free-monoid pairs () ‣ The instantiation (, and ) ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a>) and <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq\mathcal{N}(L-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq\mathcal{N}(L-1)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\lvert\hat{K}\cap\hat{K}^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N]\rvert}{N}\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\lvert\hat{K}\cap\hat{K}^{\prime}[1\!\dots\!N]\rvert}{N}\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\ \frac{\exp(O((\log\log L)^{2}))+(\log L)^{-2}\,\mathcal{N}(L)}{\mathcal{N}(L-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\ \frac{\exp(O((\log\log L)^{2}))+(\log L)^{-2}\,\mathcal{N}(L)}{\mathcal{N}(L-1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\ o(1)+(\log L)^{-2}\bigl(1+q+q\log_{2}L\bigr)\ =\ \Theta(1/\log L)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\ o(1)+(\log L)^{-2}\bigl(1+q+q\log_{2}L\bigr)\ =\ \Theta(1/\log L),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">using (<a href="#A4.E7" title="Equation D.7 ‣ Proof. ‣ Free-monoid pairs () ‣ The instantiation (, and ) ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.7</span></a>) to absorb the <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(O((\log\log L)^{2}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(O((\log\log L)^{2}))</annotation></semantics></math> term into <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o(1)</annotation></semantics></math>. The bound
(<a href="#A4.Ex14" title="In Proof. ‣ Free-monoid pairs () ‣ The instantiation (, and ) ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.8</span></a>) holds along the prefix scales <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=\mathcal{N}(L-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=\mathcal{N}(L-1)</annotation></semantics></math>; interpolating between
consecutive scales (the count grows by the factor (<a href="#A4.E4" title="Equation D.4 ‣ Proof. ‣ Free-monoid pairs () ‣ The instantiation (, and ) ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a>) between <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L-1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>)
gives the same <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o(1)</annotation></semantics></math> rate for general <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{d}(\hat{K},\hat{K}^{\prime})\ =\ 0:" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn> 0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{d}(\hat{K},\hat{K}^{\prime})\ =\ 0:</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">nested
tag-pairs under the unbounded cut realize no <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. This is why the bounded cut
<math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\equiv 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\equiv 1</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p8.3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">forced</em> for the name-cut construction shape; we present (i) as a
worked example and (ii) as its obstruction, not as a generic compressible-language theorem.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(iii) Extreme separation point.</span> For the pair <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{K},\hat{K}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{K},\hat{K}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> of (ii): run any finite-trivia sound generator against the
racing enumeration of <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{K}</annotation></semantics></math> as the revealed core. As in <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 3.6 (Impossibility side of the dichotomy). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a>(b), the same
transcript serves both truths, and <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{d}(\hat{K},\hat{K}^{\prime})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{d}(\hat{K},\hat{K}^{\prime})=0</annotation></semantics></math> forces the coverage at truth
<math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{K}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{K}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> to satisfy <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\leq\overline{d}(\hat{K},\hat{K}^{\prime})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\leq\overline{d}(\hat{K},\hat{K}^{\prime})=0</annotation></semantics></math> plus the finite-trivia correction
<math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}/N\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}/N\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>; hence coverage <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> at truth <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{K}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{K}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. On the other hand, <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\mathrm{sw}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>sw</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\mathrm{sw}}</annotation></semantics></math> of
<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem7" title="Theorem 3.7 (Achievability side: sweep and the tight generator). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.7</span></a>(i) achieves <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\geq 1-\overline{d}(C,\hat{K}^{\prime})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\geq 1-\overline{d}(C,\hat{K}^{\prime})=1</annotation></semantics></math> (since
<math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{d}(C,\hat{K}^{\prime})=\overline{d}(\hat{K},\hat{K}^{\prime})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{d}(C,\hat{K}^{\prime})=\overline{d}(\hat{K},\hat{K}^{\prime})=0</annotation></semantics></math>) with vanishing trivia rate. The free
regime thus exhibits the maximal gap of the dichotomy: coverage <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> versus <math id="A4.SS6.SSS2.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS6.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#1F4FA8;">Imprecision of exhaustive generation (<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 4.3 (Imprecision of exhaustive generation). ‣ Case Study: Instantiation in a Compression Model of Mathematics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>)</h4>

<div id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="32.78" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 670 32.78" width="670"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,32.78) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><clipPath id="pgfcp31"><path d="M -22670.54 -22670.54 L 22670.54 -22670.54 L 22670.54 22670.54 L -22670.54 22670.54 Z M 0 4.72 L 0 28.06 C 0 30.67 2.12 32.78 4.72 32.78 L 665.28 32.78 C 667.89 32.78 670 30.67 670 28.06 L 670 4.72 C 670 2.12 667.89 0 665.28 0 L 4.72 0 C 2.12 0 0 2.12 0 4.72 Z"></path></clipPath><g fill-rule="evenodd"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F3F7FC;" fill="#F3F7FC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.72 L 0 28.06 C 0 30.67 2.12 32.78 4.72 32.78 L 665.28 32.78 C 667.89 32.78 670 30.67 670 28.06 L 670 4.72 C 670 2.12 667.89 0 665.28 0 L 4.72 0 C 2.12 0 0 2.12 0 4.72 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#6284C2;--ltx-fill-color:#6284C2;--ltx-fg-color:#6284C2;" color="#6284C2" fill="#6284C2" stroke="#6284C2" stroke-width="1.5pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 1.04 32.78 L 1.04 0"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.62 12.93)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:46.45em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="642.74"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:46.45em;">
<span id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">See <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 4.3 (Imprecision of exhaustive generation). ‣ Case Study: Instantiation in a Compression Model of Mathematics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.SSS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Work in <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> with base <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\geq 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\geq 4</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa&lt;n(1-1/\log_{2}c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa&lt;n(1-1/\log_{2}c)</annotation></semantics></math>. The wrapped-length ball
<math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{G}(r)=\{w:\lvert w\rvert_{G}\leq r\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{G}(r)=\{w:\lvert w\rvert_{G}\leq r\}</annotation></semantics></math> has volume <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert B_{G}(r)\rvert=\Theta(r^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert B_{G}(r)\rvert=\Theta(r^{n})</annotation></semantics></math> (the number of
exponent vectors <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(N_{1},\dots,N_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(N_{1},\dots,N_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}N_{i}\leq r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}N_{i}\leq r</annotation></semantics></math>). By <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem7" title="Lemma D.7 (Digit-sum formula). ‣ Proof. ‣ Abelian refinement chains () ‣ The instantiation (, and ) ‣ Appendix D Deferred Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.7</span></a>, <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in H=H_{D_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in H=H_{D_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math> iff <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}s_{c}(N_{i})\leq\theta_{\kappa}(\lvert w\rvert_{G})=\kappa\log_{2}(1+\lvert w\rvert_{G})\leq\kappa\log_{2}(1+r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}s_{c}(N_{i})\leq\theta_{\kappa}(\lvert w\rvert_{G})=\kappa\log_{2}(1+\lvert w\rvert_{G})\leq\kappa\log_{2}(1+r)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Upper bound.</em><span id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text"> The number of vectors with <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}s_{c}(N_{i})\leq\kappa\log_{2}r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}s_{c}(N_{i})\leq\kappa\log_{2}r</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}N_{i}\leq r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}N_{i}\leq r</annotation></semantics></math> is at most the number of vectors whose total base-<math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> digit sum is at most
<math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\coloneqq\kappa\log_{2}r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\coloneqq\kappa\log_{2}r</annotation></semantics></math>, each coordinate <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;c^{\,L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;c^{\,L}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=\log_{c}r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=\log_{c}r</annotation></semantics></math>. A standard count
of nonnegative integer vectors with bounded digit sum gives <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert H\cap B_{G}(r)\rvert\leq c_{2}^{\prime}\,r^{\,n/\log_{2}c+\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert H\cap B_{G}(r)\rvert\leq c_{2}^{\prime}\,r^{\,n/\log_{2}c+\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> up to logarithmic factors; dividing by <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert B_{G}(r)\rvert=\Theta(r^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert B_{G}(r)\rvert=\Theta(r^{n})</annotation></semantics></math>
gives</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\lvert H\cap B_{G}(r)\rvert}{\lvert B_{G}(r)\rvert}\leq c_{2}\,r^{-\delta},\qquad\delta=n-\kappa-n/\log_{2}c&gt;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\lvert H\cap B_{G}(r)\rvert}{\lvert B_{G}(r)\rvert}\leq c_{2}\,r^{-\delta},\qquad\delta=n-\kappa-n/\log_{2}c&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> by the hypothesis <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa&lt;n(1-1/\log_{2}c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa&lt;n(1-1/\log_{2}c)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Lower bound.</em><span id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text"> Restrict to vectors all of whose coordinates are powers of <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> (digit sum
<math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> each, total <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq n\leq\kappa\log_{2}r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq n\leq\kappa\log_{2}r</annotation></semantics></math> for large <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>): there are <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta((\log_{c}r)^{n})=\Theta((\log r)^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta((\log_{c}r)^{n})=\Theta((\log r)^{n})</annotation></semantics></math> of these within <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{G}(r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{G}(r)</annotation></semantics></math>, but a stronger family gives the stated rate.
Take a single coordinate to range over base-<math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> blocks of magnitude up to <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{1/\log_{2}c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{1/\log_{2}c}</annotation></semantics></math>
(digit sum <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, the rest fixed); these lie in <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\cap B_{G}(r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\cap B_{G}(r)</annotation></semantics></math> and number <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(r^{1/\log_{2}c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(r^{1/\log_{2}c})</annotation></semantics></math>. Dividing by <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(r^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(r^{n})</annotation></semantics></math> gives <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert H\cap B_{G}(r)\rvert/\lvert B_{G}(r)\rvert\geq c_{1}\,r^{\,1/\log_{2}c-n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert H\cap B_{G}(r)\rvert/\lvert B_{G}(r)\rvert\geq c_{1}\,r^{\,1/\log_{2}c-n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">The two sides of (<a href="#S4.E2" title="Equation 4.2 ‣ Proposition 4.3 (Imprecision of exhaustive generation). ‣ Case Study: Instantiation in a Compression Model of Mathematics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>) do <em id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">not</em> have matching exponents: the upper bound
decays as <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{-\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{-\delta}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=n-\kappa-n/\log_{2}c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=n-\kappa-n/\log_{2}c</annotation></semantics></math>, while the lower bound decays
as <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{1/\log_{2}c-n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{1/\log_{2}c-n}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\neq n-1/\log_{2}c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\neq n-1/\log_{2}c</annotation></semantics></math> in general (they differ by <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa+(n-1)/\log_{2}c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa+(n-1)/\log_{2}c</annotation></semantics></math>). The bound therefore brackets the precision between two polynomial rates
without pinning it; closing the gap, determining the exact polynomial exponent, is open.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining the two sides gives (<a href="#S4.E2" title="Equation 4.2 ‣ Proposition 4.3 (Imprecision of exhaustive generation). ‣ Case Study: Instantiation in a Compression Model of Mathematics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>). The fraction is polynomially small in the
radius <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>. Interpreting <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> as ABFM’s compressed scale via <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=c^{\Theta(s)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=c^{\Theta(s)}</annotation></semantics></math> turns the
polynomial-in-<math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> decay into an exponential-in-<math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> decay (interpretation only, not used in the
bound). The exhaustive generator thus has precision tending to <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> polynomially in volume,
while the sweep generator of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem7" title="Theorem 3.7 (Achievability side: sweep and the tight generator). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.7</span></a>(i) has precision tending to <math id="A4.SS6.SSS3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Summary of Oracle and Feedback Models</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The verifier of <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem4" title="Definition 2.4 (Verifier oracle). ‣ The nested model: validity versus value ‣ The Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a> is one of several side-information channels studied in
this line, and the channels are not interchangeable: what a generator can learn depends
sharply on <em id="A5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">what the oracle answers about</em>. We tabulate the channels in
<a href="#A5.T2" title="In Appendix E Summary of Oracle and Feedback Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> along the axis that organizes our results, namely whether the oracle speaks
about the unknown target or about a fixed superset.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.2" class="ltx_logical-block">
      
<figure id="A5.T2" class="ltx_table ltx_align_center">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A5.T2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="A5.T2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Side-information channels in the generation-in-the-limit line. The
ambient oracle of this paper is the only one that answers about a fixed
<em id="A5.T2.5.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">superset</em> of the target rather than about the target or the collection.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
      
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
