<td id="A5.p2.1.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">
<span id="A5.p2.1.7.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:93.2pt;">
<span id="A5.p2.1.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">computational traces / richer observations <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">Peng et al., 2026</a>; <a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">Papazov and Flammarion, 2025</a>)</cite></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A5.p2.1.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">
<span id="A5.p2.1.7.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:103.5pt;">
<span id="A5.p2.1.7.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">execution traces of the accepting machine; time-bounded observations of the algorithm</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A5.p2.1.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">
<span id="A5.p2.1.7.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:113.9pt;">
<span id="A5.p2.1.7.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">restores identification beyond input–output data (Chomsky hierarchy; learning algorithms)</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.p2.1.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.p2.1.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">
<span id="A5.p2.1.8.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:93.2pt;">
<span id="A5.p2.1.8.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">classical MQ<math id="A5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}+{}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}+{}</annotation></semantics></math>EQ / oracle-aided inference <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Angluin, 1987</a>; <a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Angluin, 1988</a>; <a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gasarch and Pleszkoch, 1989</a>; <a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Stephan, 1998</a>)</cite></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A5.p2.1.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">
<span id="A5.p2.1.8.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:103.5pt;">
<span id="A5.p2.1.8.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">membership / equivalence to the target; Turing-degree oracles</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A5.p2.1.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">
<span id="A5.p2.1.8.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:113.9pt;">
<span id="A5.p2.1.8.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">identification of the target from queries</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.p2.1.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.p2.1.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">
<span id="A5.p2.1.9.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:93.2pt;">
<span id="A5.p2.1.9.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p2.1.9.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">this paper</span>: ambient membership <math id="A5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A5.p2.1.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">
<span id="A5.p2.1.9.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:103.5pt;">
<span id="A5.p2.1.9.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">is <math id="A5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> formally valid (in <math id="A5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A5.p2.1.9.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">
<span id="A5.p2.1.9.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:113.9pt;">
<span id="A5.p2.1.9.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">validity for free, breadth unchanged (<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1 (Verification is not taste). ‣ Verification is not taste ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>); sound coverage enabled (<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 3.2 (The exhaustive generator and the separation). ‣ Sound coverage: what the verifier does buy ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>); dichotomy unaffected (<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem10" title="Corollary 3.10 (The trivia dichotomy). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Corollary</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.10</span></a> is verifier-free)</span>
</span></td></tr>
</table>
</div>
    
</div>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The placement of our oracle is the source of every result. Because <math id="A5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> returns
“valid” on all of <math id="A5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> and never supplies a negative inside the grey zone <math id="A5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\setminus H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\setminus H</annotation></semantics></math>, it is <em id="A5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">informationless within a fiber</em>: two candidates sharing one ambient receive
identical answers, which is exactly why it cannot move the Angluin boundary
(<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1 (Verification is not taste). ‣ Verification is not taste ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>). Yet <em id="A5.p3.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">across</em> ambients the same oracle is decisive: it identifies the
formal world, which is all the verifier contributes to breadth and all that sound coverage
needs (<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 3.2 (The exhaustive generator and the separation). ‣ Sound coverage: what the verifier does buy ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Numerical Validation</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The main results of the paper are purely theoretical. This appendix records the simulations
that sanity-checked the density claims and the two arithmetic traps a naive implementation
falls into.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Methodology.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Coverage is a property of the <em id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">limit set</em> (<a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Fact 2.1 (Partial-enumeration generation; ( , , Theorem 1.6 in arXiv version)). ‣ Partial enumeration and the revealed core ‣ The Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fact</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>, following KW’s
Definition 1.1), not of any finite stage, so a simulation must fix the prefix size <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> and
grow the run length <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> until the measured coverage stabilizes. Reading coverage at the run
frontier (where the prefix and the horizon advance together) systematically
<em id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">under-reads</em>, because the sweep has not yet claimed the never-enumerated valuable
elements within <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H[1\!\dots\!N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H[1\!\dots\!N]</annotation></semantics></math>: a fixed-<math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> series at <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1/3</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=999" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>999</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=999</annotation></semantics></math> read <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.263\to 0.480\to 0.830" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.263</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0.480</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0.830</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.263\to 0.480\to 0.830</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> grew to <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\cdot 10^{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\cdot 10^{5}</annotation></semantics></math>, converging only once <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\gg N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≫</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\gg N</annotation></semantics></math>. Second,
membership in <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> must be computed in <em id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">exact rational arithmetic</em>. With floating point,
<math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lceil 42/0.7\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mn>42</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>0.7</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lceil 42/0.7\rceil</annotation></semantics></math> evaluates from <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="60.00000000000001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>60.00000000000001</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">60.00000000000001</annotation></semantics></math> and misclassifies the boundary
element; at <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.7</annotation></semantics></math> this manufactured spurious counterexamples to the density identity
(<a href="#S3.E2" title="Equation 3.2 ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>) that exact arithmetic dissolves.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">The tight family at <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1/3</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A6.T3" title="In The tight family at 𝛼=1/3. ‣ Appendix F Numerical Validation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> reports coverage of <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and of two control generators against the
racing adversary <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. The race share converges to <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2</annotation></semantics></math>, the truth-<math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> coverage
of <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\alpha/2=5/6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\alpha/2=5/6</annotation></semantics></math>, and a pure conjunction race (the finite-trivia
representative) stalls at <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha/2</annotation></semantics></math>. The naive <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>-sweeper that omits the race covers
exactly <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, confirming that the race/sweep split is load-bearing: dropping the race
loses exactly the half-of-<math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> contribution.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_logical-block">
        
<figure id="A6.T3" class="ltx_table ltx_align_center">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A6.T3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="A6.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Tight family <math id="A6.T3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.T3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1/3</annotation></semantics></math>, racing adversary <math id="A6.T3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>. Measured
coverage (fixed <math id="A6.T3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, grown <math id="A6.T3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>) against the proven limit. The trivia counts confirm
<math id="A6.T3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lfloor\sqrt{T}\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em" stretchy="true">⌊</mo><msqrt><mi>T</mi></msqrt><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em" stretchy="true">⌋</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lfloor\sqrt{T}\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math> trivia at truth <math id="A6.T3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> (rate <math id="A6.T3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>) and zero at truth <math id="A6.T3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
        
<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">Generator</td>
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">Truth</td>
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> (or <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>)</td>
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">Measured</td>
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">Predicted limit</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=10^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=10^{3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.4930" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.4930</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.4930</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=10^{4},\ T=4.5\cdot 10^{7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4.5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=10^{4},\ T=4.5\cdot 10^{7}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.8317" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.8317</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.8317</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left"><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\alpha/2=5/6\approx 0.8333" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.8333</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\alpha/2=5/6\approx 0.8333</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">pure conj. race</td>
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">—</td>
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1702" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1702</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1702</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left"><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha/2\approx 0.1667" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.1667</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha/2\approx 0.1667</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">naive <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>-sweep (no race)</td>
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">—</td>
