</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Other densities.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A6.T4" title="In Other densities. ‣ Appendix F Numerical Validation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> reports the truth-<math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> coverage of <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> across <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, measured at <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=10^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=10^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. Convergence is to <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\alpha/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\alpha/2</annotation></semantics></math> from below, and slows as <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> (the
small-<math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> deficit is dominated by the <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\sqrt{N})/N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\sqrt{N})/N</annotation></semantics></math> race correction, which is largest
relative to the tiny <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha/2</annotation></semantics></math> race contribution).</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.1" class="ltx_logical-block">
        
<figure id="A6.T4" class="ltx_table ltx_align_center">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A6.T4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 4</span>: </span><math id="A6.T4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">G</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{*}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.T4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> truth-<math id="A6.T4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> coverage at <math id="A6.T4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=10^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=10^{3}</annotation></semantics></math> across densities. The <math id="A6.T4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.01</annotation></semantics></math>
row needed <math id="A6.T4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\approx 3\cdot 10^{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\approx 3\cdot 10^{6}</annotation></semantics></math> to stabilize; the others converge faster.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
        
<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">Measured</td>
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">Predicted <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\alpha/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\alpha/2</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.7</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.644" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.644</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.644</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.65" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.65</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.65</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.99</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.99</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.503" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.503</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.503</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left"><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.505" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.505</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.505</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.01</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.994" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.994</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.994</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.995" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.995</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.995</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
</div>
      
</div>
<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In every run convergence approaches the proven limit from below, with a deficit consistent
with the <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\sqrt{N})/N+O(\log N)/N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\sqrt{N})/N+O(\log N)/N</annotation></semantics></math> corrections of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem7" title="Theorem 3.7 (Achievability side: sweep and the tight generator). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorems</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.7</span></a> and <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 3.6 (Impossibility side of the dichotomy). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a>; and hostile
enumeration orders breached no bound (a deliberately delaying order read <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5260\geq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.5260</mn><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5260\geq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math> at
truth <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, on the correct side of the cap).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>The Dichotomy by Hand: A Worked Miniature</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The race lemma and the two ends of the dichotomy can be watched in twenty rounds. Take the
tight family (<a href="#S3.E1" title="Equation 3.1 ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>) at <math id="A7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1/2</annotation></semantics></math>: the coverable world is the evens <math id="A7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}=\{0,2,4,\dots\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}=\{0,2,4,\dots\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the revealed target is every second even, <math id="A7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=\{2,6,10,\dots\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=\{2,6,10,\dots\}</annotation></semantics></math>
(the residue <math id="A7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\bmod 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>mod</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\bmod 4</annotation></semantics></math>), the difference is <math id="A7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\{0,4,8,\dots\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\{0,4,8,\dots\}</annotation></semantics></math> (the residue <math id="A7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\bmod 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>mod</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\bmod 4</annotation></semantics></math>), and the ambient is <math id="A7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, so the odds sit idle throughout: neither player ever
touches them. The adversary is the racing adversary <math id="A7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Definition 3.4 (The racing adversary). ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>, which
enumerates fresh <math id="A7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prec" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≺</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prec</annotation></semantics></math>-least elements of <math id="A7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> except at rounds <math id="A7.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=2^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=2^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, where it
re-enumerates an element the generator has already claimed. The generator is the tight
generator <math id="A7.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> of (<a href="#S3.E4" title="Equation 3.4 ‣ The tight family. ‣ The trivia phase transition ‣ Main Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>), which sweeps the union <math id="A7.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{t}=K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{t}=K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> at square rounds <math id="A7.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in R=\{1,4,9,16,\dots\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in R=\{1,4,9,16,\dots\}</annotation></semantics></math> and races the intersection <math id="A7.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{t}=K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{t}=K</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise. Within a
round the adversary moves first; the generator sees <math id="A7.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<a href="#A7.T5" title="In Appendix G The Dichotomy by Hand: A Worked Miniature" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> replays the first twenty rounds; the trace, the prefix counts, and the
coverage figures below are machine-generated and machine-checked.</p>
</div>
